{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod","id":1050909,"title":"Many WoDs vs. Single WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-18T00:51:04-08:00","id":1050909,"title":"Many WoDs vs. Single WoD","content":"This is an argument that has a way of derailing threads, I thought I'd give it its own thread. Of course, this thread already addressed the &quot;how&quot; of treating the WoD as a single setting:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod\"> History lessons - how to fit everything in the cWoD - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1033861-history-lessons-how-to-fit-everything-in-the-cwod </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Impergium, the great flood, the first and second citties, the Fae war of the courts, the sundering of changelling, the great Maelstroms, the Rage wars, the anarchist revolt, the advent of reason, the rise of the Consensus, the creation of the Camarilla and Sabbatt, the birth of the Tremere and Giovanni, the council of the 9 Traditions, the rise of the Technocratic Union, the Inquisition, the destruction of Charon, the destruction of the Bunyup... How can anyone mix all this toghether? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The current thread is for the &quot;whys&quot; and &quot;why nots&quot;.<br /> <br /> See, I've always felt that treating each gameline as a separate universe was one canonical way to run a game. I'll call this the Many WoDs Model (MWM).<br /> <br /> Likewise, treating the whole thing as a &quot;Rashomon&quot; in which each perspective is half true and the goal for any given play group is to decide which half is another interpretation that's contradicted an supported about as much. I'll call this the Single WoD Model (SWM).<br /> <br /> Conversely, I keep finding myself in conversations with WoD players on- and offline where we're going around comparing notes and brainstorming about how to run a certain aspect of the setting, and someone (often I) will propose some interpretation that cross-references things from two different games. Most often, this involves bringing up Consensus or the Triat outside of Mage or Werewolf, respectively.<br /> <br /> This will prompt someone to explain that this sort of cross-referencing is simply not the correct way to read canon. Instead, the bits where, say, a werewolf shows up in a Mage book and something about the Wyrm are to be taken as some sort of authorial wink and nothing more. If a mage shows up in a Werewolf: the Apocalypse game, he's a Werewolf-style mage whose powers rely entirely on Werewolf metaphysics.<br /> <br /> The given reasoning is typically that questioning the cosmology of the gameline that the players think they're playing is an ST bait-and-switch. A player who sits down for a Mage game isn't expecting some Triat to be more important than Consensus.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it's claimed, the correct way to include werewolves in a Mage game is to come up with some simplified versions of werewolves who follow Mage rules and are probably subject to Paradox and know nothing the Triat or Pentex.<br /> <br /> My response to this is that is that (for an extreme example) if I'm starting a Mage game and a player hands me a character sheet with &quot;Werewolf Lore OOOOO&quot; on it, and I allow it, I should see that player hold up a flag that says &quot;I'm a fan of Werewolf: the Apocalypse, and I want you to incorporate themes and elements from Werewolf: the Apocalypse into your Mage game, so my character can shine by having access to most of my OOC knowledge about werewolves.&quot;<br /> <br /> That &quot;Werewolf Lore OOOOO&quot; flag does not say &quot;I want you to take me aside and explain to me your homebrew Mage-style-werewolves, which my fan-obsession tells me almost nothing about.&quot;<br /> <br /> The latter seems much more like a bait-and-switch to me than the former.<br /> <br /> Amber the worst part is that these denouncements tend to occur in discussions that are already explicitly about crossovers. This makes the very notion of discussing crossovers confusing for me. It seems like in order to be coherent we would have to make very clear from the beginning whether, for instance, we were discussing a Vampire/Demon crossover from a vampire's point of view or from a demon's point of view. If we have to adhere to the MWM there is no general World of Darkness to discuss in this forum. There are seven Worlds of Darkness, each of which may contain its own vague theme park versions of any combination of the others.<br /> <br /> I'd like to know what actual experiences people have had in-game that have turned them on or off to either model, and what evidence there is that either is significantly more canonical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T13:40:17-08:00","id":1051128,"title":"","content":"I always use a one cWoD world because that is how it is written in the books, especially in 2nd edition and Revised. It gives me, the ST, enormous resources for my games and it prevents my players from getting bored because they will never know what I will be throwing against them. Anyway, that is how I have been playing cWoD since 1993, so I have no reason to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T20:22:43-08:00","id":1051336,"title":"","content":"I've always used the &quot;Many WoD in one WoD&quot; model when I run a game. When I run Mage, Mage cosmology is correct. When I run Werewolf, Werewolf cosmology is correct. When I run Demon, Demon cosmology is correct. When I run Kindred of the East, KotE cosmology is correct.<br /> <br /> So a player in a Mage game takes Werewolf Lore at 5 dots or whatever. His character knows what those Werewolves believe, but he also knows that tall their myths about Gaia and everything are just mistakes, reality doesn't work like that. Likewise, if I'm running a Werewolf game and someone has, Awakened Lore at 5 dots, they know Mages believes in consensual reality, but <i>obviously</i> those guys are completely wrong - Gaia and werewolves were around long before humans.<br /> <br /> Everyone lives in the same world, and everyone has their own beliefs. Everyone can also prove their own beliefs in their own way and the world operates differently for different groups. The world is, in essence, less like a single tapestry and more like a quilt sewn together by many different people, and so in some way they are all equally right and wrong. When I'm running a game for a specific group, then that group is obviously going to be &quot;more right&quot; when it comes to cosmology than everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T23:14:33-08:00","id":1051387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1051128#post1051128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always use a one cWoD world because that is how it is written in the books, especially in 2nd edition and Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>No<br /> it<br /> is<br /> not.</b></i><br /> <br /> I've posted this before, but let me do it again: The <i>Revised Storyteller's Guide </i>literally writes<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pg. 174, under &quot;Drawing Distinctions</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In its design, <b>Vampire</b> is intended to be played as a stand-alone game. The various factions, groups and subcultures prevalent in other games from the Storyteller series <u>quite simply do not exist</u> if you\u2019re playing <b>Vampire</b> exclusively. Vampire has no Silent Striders, no Technocracy and no Unseelie Court</div> </div> </div> </div>Underlined emphasis mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T01:05:41-08:00","id":1051409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1051387#post1051387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i><b>No<br /> it<br /> is<br /> not.</b></i><br /> <br /> I've posted this before, but let me do it again: The <i>Revised Storyteller's Guide </i>literally writesUnderlined emphasis mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> <i>See what I mean?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire Revised Storyteller's Guide, pg. 174</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In its design, Vampire is intended to be played as a stand-alone game. The various factions, groups and subcultures prevalent in other games from the Storyteller series quite simply do not exist <u>if you\u2019re playing Vampire exclusively</u>. Vampire has no Silent Striders, no Technocracy and no Unseelie Court</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> There are crossover sections in every corebook except Demon, as well as many sourcebooks. There are crossover references in most books. There are crossover rules. There are sample NPCs in books that aren't of their home gameline. Every game has at least one splat associated with fae and one associated with wraiths. Vampire has the Thaumaturgy path of Spirit Manipulation and the Ahrimane bloodline, even though Vampire generally doesn't address the Umbra. There are numerous major metaplot points that involve crossovers, particularly the Week of Nightmares, which had repercussions for every game that were given no other explanation. <br /> <br /> The option to keep them separate is given, but it doesn't involve disregarding any less of canon than the alternatives do.<br /> <br /> This is my problem: I read a bunch of WoD books, and I thought the contradictions were supposed to be mysteries for groups to answer for themselves in-game. But every time I sit down to play a game, I feel bored, because we're just supposed to decide from the start that one version of one cosmology is true and anyone who contradicts it must accept out of game that their character is ultimately wrong, or they're breaking the fourth wall.<br /> <br /> Even within individual games, so many basic things make so little sense that it breaks my suspension of disbelief if my character is automatically wrong for questioning them.<br /> <br /> Out of all the vampires in the world, no bloodline got to 14th gen until the 20th century?<br /> <br /> The Black Spiral Dancers are universally nihilistic degenerate delusional drug addicted sociopaths, and yet they're the most successful tribe there is? <br /> <br /> Consensus rules all, but physics and technological advancement seem to proceed basically like they do IRL, at least superficially? And my Mage character is wrong not to believe that, even if he's been to the Dreaming (which is specifically canon in Mage without reference to Changeling if you go by the Book of Worlds) and seen what absolute consensus reality would actually looks like?<br /> <br /> I guess if I had to pick one cosmology, I'd rather play in, for instance, a game where the PCs are all werewolves who gradually discover to their horror that they're in a Mage game, and their hateful little religion is just that, the BSDS aren't actually much worse than the other tribes (not that that's saying much), and future Garou will remember the current &quot;apocalypse&quot; as just another War of Rage.<br /> <br /> I feel like that Werewolf game would have more Lovecraftian appeal than any tentacled Wyrm beastie. <br /> <br /> These are supposed to be games about monsters. That doesn't work if you have to take all their excuses for thinking they're not monsters at face value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5553,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","user":"Mr. Sluagh","date":". 02-19-2017, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T10:00:35-08:00","id":1051559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1051336#post1051336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always used the &quot;Many WoD in one WoD&quot; model when I run a game. When I run Mage, Mage cosmology is correct. When I run Werewolf, Werewolf cosmology is correct. When I run Demon, Demon cosmology is correct. When I run Kindred of the East, KotE cosmology is correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I run it.<br /> <br /> Adding to that: if I am running a crossover game, then I will decide in advance specifics on the cosmology. But I don't worry about informing the players. There is a very decent chance though that it never comes up in game since that would require the characters end up in a spot where the metaphysics of the different games would clash. And stuff like that usually doesn't come up without having sufficiently advanced characters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T11:57:03-08:00","id":1051599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1051409#post1051409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess if I had to pick one cosmology, I'd rather play in, for instance, a game where the PCs are all werewolves who gradually discover to their horror that they're in a Mage game, and their hateful little religion is just that</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a religion. It's a pact with beings left over from the dawn of time who were cut off from the solid, physical world, many of whom had a hand in the genesis of werewolves to begin with. Even Mage wouldn't go so far as to cut that out, most likely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the BSDS aren't actually much worse than the other tribes (not that that's saying much) </div> </div> </div>Mage would probably treat the Spiral Labyrinth as a kind of caul, which means that they're &quot;Nephandic&quot; werewolves, which is substantially worse since they might drag mages back and try to convert them into barabbi instead of just tearing them apart and letting their Avatars reincarnate normally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and future Garou will remember the current &quot;apocalypse&quot; as just another War of Rage. </div> </div> </div>Technically where the game is already headed, except that the Wars of Rage were between shapeshifters. Mokole, as witnesses to a prior struggle, would describe it as a WonderWork of the Dissolver, and might be the only ones left over to give it any kind of name to begin with. Just a little bit of history repeating...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like that Werewolf game would have more Lovecraftian appeal than any tentacled Wyrm beastie. </div> </div> </div>Have you read the Rokea book, or the material on the Chulorviah? It already has quite a great deal of that, especially since the monsters aren't affected by human belief in the least. Thunderwyrms may seem absurd to the logic of humanity, but it doesn't keep them from pulling a Tremors on isolated towns in the western US. Which is probably why there are fewer small human settlements in the WoD, come to think of it; it's not just the Impergium's long-standing effects on stress and the psyche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are supposed to be games about monsters. That doesn't work if you have to take all their excuses for thinking they're not monsters at face value. </div> </div> </div>The thing is, it's not that they're saying they aren't monsters, it's that they're saying being a monster can be alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:59:33-08:00","id":1051692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1051599#post1051599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a religion. It's a pact with beings left over from the dawn of time who were cut off from the solid, physical world, many of whom had a hand in the genesis of werewolves to begin with. Even Mage wouldn't go so far as to cut that out, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but don't a lot of religions IRL make some convoluted argument that they're not really religions because their gods are real? <br /> <br /> It's understandable to think that the reality of spirits in Werewolf lends legitimacy to Garou ideology. But on the contrary, it seems to me that if the totems are literal, finite, fallible beings whom Garou are actually in touch with, that reduces Garou beliefs to just another political ideology, more than it elevates them to a &quot;true religion&quot;.<br /> <br /> The only entities I would really call &quot;gods&quot; in the religious sense in Werewolf are Gaia and the Triat, and I think I'd have about as much trouble proving, from within the CWoD, that Gaia and the Triad literally exist, as I would have proving the Christian God exists IRL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage would probably treat the Spiral Labyrinth as a kind of caul, which means that they're &quot;Nephandic&quot; werewolves, which is substantially worse since they might drag mages back and try to convert them into barabbi instead of just tearing them apart and letting their Avatars reincarnate normally. </div> </div> </div>Okay, bad example, though I'd hazard that going with any of the other games' cosmologies would work better for what I said. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you read the Rokea book, or the material on the Chulorviah? It already has quite a great deal of that, especially since the monsters aren't affected by human belief in the least. Thunderwyrms may seem absurd to the logic of humanity, but it doesn't keep them from pulling a Tremors on isolated towns in the western US. Which is probably why there are fewer small human settlements in the WoD, come to think of it; it's not just the Impergium's long-standing effects on stress and the psyche. </div> </div> </div>Yes, like I said, Consensus clearly isn't everything, even in Mage. Mages are wrong, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, it's not that they're saying they aren't monsters, it's that they're saying being a monster can be alright. </div> </div> </div>And that, right there, is exactly my problem. <br /> <br /> It's just a matter of taste, but know what show I really hate? <i>Friends</i>. It's a show about six awful people who constantly hurt each other and everyone around them. (If you don't believe me, watch this Cracked.com video: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/n1BQ3bbJO_kh\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/n1BQ3bbJO_kh</a>)<br /> <br /> And yet, it's played as if you're supposed to like these people. You're supposed to sympathize with Ross' narcissistic self-pity, and believe that Joey is just a harmless player and Phoebe is just a loveable goofball, and laugh at Gunther along with the six &quot;friends&quot;.<br /> <br /> The antidote to <i>Friends</i> is <i>It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia</i>. It's in many ways similar to Friends, except it's up front about the fact that all characters are bad people. For instance, Dennis, the closest Joey analog, is heavily implied to a full-blown serial rapist. You're supposed to laugh at the way he and the other characters rationalize this, rather than laughing with him for being such a loveable rogue.<br /> <br /> When I try to play World of Darkness games, I usually feel like all the other players think their characters are Friends characters, and I keep wanting to break it to them that,<br /> <br /> No, I'm sorry:<br /> <br /> Your vampire character is secretly Dennis.<br /> Your werewolf character is secretly Mac.<br /> Your mage character is secretly Frank.<br /> Your wraith character is secretly Dee.<br /> Your changeling character is secretly Charlie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5553,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","user":"Mr. Sluagh","date":".  Wow, that was sure the wrong YouTube link. How did that happen? 02-19-2017, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T19:45:07-08:00","id":1051815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1051692#post1051692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but don't a lot of religions IRL make some convoluted argument that they're not really religions because their gods are real?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. They're of the same substance as those beings. They're kin supporting kin stranded in another world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's understandable to think that the reality of spirits in Werewolf lends legitimacy to Garou ideology. But on the contrary, it seems to me that if the totems are literal, finite, fallible beings whom Garou are actually in touch with, that reduces Garou beliefs to just another political ideology, more than it elevates them to a &quot;true religion&quot;. </div> </div> </div>That's not wholly inaccurate, but misses a lot of the essence of a fundamental divide between spirit and flesh. Spirits are finite, but much larger than humans, especially when you get to powerful Jagglings. Totems, which are Incarnae, are barely able to express their transcendent world view with beings of human like. Spirits are also typically operating as parts of a much larger whole, and know it, so they're somewhat less likely to engage in power plays than humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only entities I would really call &quot;gods&quot; in the religious sense in Werewolf are Gaia and the Triat, and I think I'd have about as much trouble proving, from within the CWoD, that Gaia and the Triad literally exist, as I would have proving the Christian God exists IRL. </div> </div> </div>That's what the Gnosis trait is about. If you have it, you can feel the soul of the world and communicate with it. If you don't have it, all of this will seem very strange and unrelatable, and you won't be a part of that world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, bad example, though I'd hazard that going with any of the other games' cosmologies would work better for what I said. </div> </div> </div>Certainly not Vampire or Wraith. Vampire bothers even less with questions about layers of reality, and Wraith has an Underworld shaped primarily by an attempt to make everything as horrible as possible, with any paradises promised in human belief a distant, potentially false hope. Also, there are things in the Labyrinth undreamt of by humanity's wildest imaginations; whole worlds passed into it with enough death and destruction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, like I said, Consensus clearly isn't everything, even in Mage. Mages are wrong, too. </div> </div> </div>That seems like it would completely undermine your position in an argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that, right there, is exactly my problem.<br /> <br /> It's just a matter of taste, but know what show I really hate? <i>Friends</i>. It's a show about s... </div> </div> </div>I'm not following your pop culture references. I'll just be over with the Gene Wilder Wonka punishing sinners in hilariously, if viciously, ironic fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T22:35:55-08:00","id":1051866,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are dark and tragic heroes that are more angry and more spiritually aware that any other major supernatural creature. Fera (or Kinfolk) with Gnosis 1 are more connected to Gaia (and Nature) than any Changeling, Kindred, KJ, Mage, Wraith, etc could ever hope to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T23:57:08-08:00","id":1051879,"title":"","content":"In first edition, it is very apparent that everything is supposed to be the one world and one game line. Crossover was not a dirty word and it was expected. Each game line has all these crossover hooks embedded into it (Malkavians with Fae, Giovanni with Wraith, Tremere with Mage, Silent Striders with Wraith, Fianna with Fae, Dreamspeakers with Garou, etc.) However, very quickly it became apparent that 1) game mechanics were not compatible as each game line used its own attributes, and 2) increasingly different editorial visions produced more and more buffer between the various games. The second problem was probably more crucial than the first.<br /> <br /> People who claim that this was always so because of statements made in late second edition or revised should know the game's history a little bit better,<br /> <br /> To me, it is one World of Darkness, and as an ST I have to figure out how it all blends together. There are lots of things I disagree with in each game line, so I'm already editing it to various degrees. This is just one more edit. Of course, if you only play one game and don't read the others, there is no reason for you to do so either.<br /> <br /> Simply because in real life the various developers and editors of the 5 game lines couldn't make it work because of their egos and different visions doesn't mean I have that problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T01:06:04-08:00","id":1051891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1051879#post1051879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In first edition, it is very apparent that everything is supposed to be the one world and one game line. Crossover was not a dirty word and it was expected. Each game line has all these crossover hooks embedded into it (Malkavians with Fae, Giovanni with Wraith, Tremere with Mage, Silent Striders with Wraith, Fianna with Fae, Dreamspeakers with Garou, etc.) However, very quickly it became apparent that 1) game mechanics were not compatible as each game line used its own attributes, and 2) increasingly different editorial visions produced more and more buffer between the various games. The second problem was probably more crucial than the first.<br /> <br /> People who claim that this was always so because of statements made in late second edition or revised should know the game's history a little bit better,</div> </div> </div> </div>Did the mages that showed up in other games actually end up like the mages in Mage? Because I get the distinct impression from hearing the criticisms of Mage across the years that its earliest iteration was not particularly keen on playing well with others, and that post-modernism was never really a thing in the other games. Even if they had hooks, that's about all they practically had. Late 2nd edition to Revised is just coming to terms with the reality that they didn't mesh well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, it is one World of Darkness, and as an ST I have to figure out how it all blends together. There are lots of things I disagree with in each game line, so I'm already editing it to various degrees. This is just one more edit. Of course, if you only play one game and don't read the others, there is no reason for you to do so either.<br /> <br /> Simply because in real life the various developers and editors of the 5 game lines couldn't make it work because of their egos and different visions doesn't mean I have that problem. </div> </div> </div>I doubt that it was much to do with egos, and more to do with the core theses of the games, which became dramatically different, and created setting lore that was keen to roll downhill and collect more snow on its own path, away from the others. None perhaps moreso than Mage, which, as noted, has very particular ideas about what is and isn't that don't even come close to meshing at all with other games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:30:05-08:00","id":1051972,"title":"","content":"It has to do with the core concept of the games(subjective reality it's a big thing in Mage), egos (the need to rewrite the world arround your game, as can be seen by the appropiation of all the cool history figures by one game or another), and the impossibility to know a canon that expands trough hundreds of books without being a full time geek (and even then it's hard).<br /> <br /> Rather than make the effort of creating a crossover WoD corebook, that will not only be massive, but also will make fans of every game angry, the authors decided to never adress this kind of issues. Or at least that was, more or less, the reason that Satyros comented when he refused to do an all encompassing Book of the Crossover when it was suggested to him in facebook, back when M20 was still being written.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want to do so, there are sufficent connections to do it, but then don't go arround telling others &quot;how WoD <i>really</i> works&quot; when your view of WoD colides with that of other fans (something more than common, as each one has it's own view of how &quot;everything makes perfect sense&quot;).<br /> <br /> This it's why in 3rd edition the &quot;others&quot; are always shown in an antagonistic light. No more the Gangrel are friends with Garou, the relationships between Malkavian and the Fae are all but forgotten...etc. Notably, you can't see the 3 points Merit &quot;Supernatural Friend&quot; anywhere. This it's a buffer that discourages including PLAYER characters (the ones that care about their methaphysics being right) in the games, while alowing the ST to introduce them as npc, which are rarely so conflictive about the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-20-2017, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T11:54:51-08:00","id":1052080,"title":"","content":"To me it's very simple: there are a ton of connections between the games, in every level, from sourcebooks to chronicles to novels etc. <br /> <br /> The games are assuming a splat-only play style as default, but that's for the sake of convenience/thematic 'pureness' and as mentioned, the writers' view on the games. It was simply easier to do it this way for WW (although I firmly believe that in the meantime they missed a lot of potential).<br /> <br /> However, again, the WoD itself is undoubtedly a crossover setting to me. Even the brand itself is &quot;World of Darkness&quot;, not &quot;Worlds of Darkness&quot; and every game is a part of it and again, crossover is supported with story and rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:30:57-08:00","id":1052261,"title":"","content":"No one is forcing anyone to play or run a crossover game, it is just that the setting supports crossover games even if the game mechanics are poor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:57:55-08:00","id":1052280,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: These are impressions and experiences relating to the topic and not my beliefs.<br /> <br /> In my very first Vampire the Masquerade session, I saw that the ST had a Werewolf the Apocalypse book. I looked them over, noting how the character sheets looked similar. The ST told me &quot;They are actually in the same universe!&quot; in a very excited tone. I thought that was cool. I asked her to play one. Her expression went from excited to dour. &quot;No, we're playing Vampire.&quot; she said. Being 13, I took this as some kind of unfair remark, and was a jerky kid about the whole thing. The ST herself didn't seem to realize why she was saying no, which only incensed me further. I chose to, obviously, play a Gangrel. Because that's what you do.<br /> <br /> After that I played in and ran a lot of crossover games, then stopped after a couple years. A long time later, with the benefit of hindsight and design experience under my belt, I understand why she reacted that way, even if she or I didn't at the time. It was in defense of thematic integrity of the given game, and the difficulties of undermining it for crossover. Whether it was intended to be run one way or another was immaterial to us, given that crossovers just didn't seem to work mechanically either.<br /> <br /> Another impression I got was being anti-crossover was sort of an identity issue for some early players. One of the ways in which White Wolf games were supposed to be different from DnD, which, back then, was kind of a selling point was to NOT be the colorful troupe of mixed race adventurers. It was something else. You were monsters, of a stripe. The impression I got was trying to turn the game into something of a splat-troupe was seen as kind of an amateurish or dick move, spotlight hogging, etc.<br /> <br /> In any case, I prefer MWM. Based on my experiences, it would be weirder if I didn't.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T00:55:01-08:00","id":1052433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1051879#post1051879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who claim that this was always so because of statements made in late second edition or revised should know the game's history a little bit better,</div> </div> </div> </div>You are absolutely correct, and I agree.<br /> <br /> Because it was <u><i>late</i> <i>&quot;Second Edition</i></u>&quot; that was lousy with crazy crossover stuff.<br /> <br /> So let me elucidate:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In first edition, it is very apparent that everything is supposed to be the one world and one game line. Crossover was not a dirty word and it was expected. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Crossover was not a dirty word&quot; since crossover <i>didn't exist</i> - because <b>which</b> &quot;first edition?&quot; The only two books that share an overlap in first editions are <i>Vampire</i> (1991) and <i>Werewolf</i> (1992) - <i>Vampire 2nd</i> <i>edition</i> (1992) was published a year before <i>Mage 1st</i> <i>edition</i> even hit the shelves (1993). <i>Vampire 1e</i> didn't have any crossover stuff because <i>there was nothing to crossover with</i>. In fact, <i>V:TM 2e</i> was published a month after <i>W:TA 1e</i> (May and June, respectively), so <u>even then</u>, their overlap was only ~30 days. 1994 saw the publication of <i>Wraith 1e</i> and <i>Werewolf 2e</i>, then <i>Changeling 1e</i> and <i>Mage 2e</i> in 1995. <i>Wraith 2e</i> was published in 1996, and <i>Changeling 2e</i> in 1997, so I don't know where you're getting this nebulous &quot;1st edition/2nd edition&quot; divide - there's no clear-cut delineation like there is in something like D&amp;D or Shadowrun, not until the <i>Revised</i> era in 1998 starting with <i>Vampire</i> (and <i>Werewolf</i> and <i>Mage</i> both published in 2000).<br /> <br /> Infamously, it was 1996's <i>The Risen</i> (published for <i>Wraith 2e</i>) that said &quot;make sure you have a copy of <i>Vampire 2e</i> on hand for Potence, Celerity, Fortitude, and Obfuscate!&quot; and 1997's <i>Charnel Houses of Europe </i>that ran a disclaimer stating &quot;anything in this book supersedes material published in <i>Berlin by Night</i> (1993).&quot; <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</i> was also published in December of 1994, only a few months after <i>Wraith 1e</i>, but a book for <i>Vampire 2e</i>. <b>All of the rubbish crossover stuff was mid-to-late Second Edition <i>Vampire</i> </b>mostly (excluding the Week of Nightmares and Red Sign stuff, which was rubbish <i>Revised Era</i> stuff, though <i>Blood Treachery</i> (2000) and <i>Ghost Towns</i> (1998) were good).<br /> <br /> And let's not even get into the Tremere and Order of Hermes with their connection to <i>Ars Magica</i> - a game not owned by White Wolf or even part of the World of Darkness, but published by them - or how Exalted was originally advertised as the &quot;pre-history&quot; of the World of Darkness (or that there was a real-life wrestler going by the name Gangrel...).<br /> <br /> It was the <i>Revised Era</i> that said &quot;We're getting too silly. Everyone back to your corners <i>like we were in the beginning</i>.&quot; 1994-98 was the time of &quot;FishMalks&quot; and Sam Haight, when Vampire gained the derogatory label of &quot;vampions,&quot; and Garou were referred to as &quot;Captain Planet wannabees.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, there's a(/several) reason(s) why the Antagonists chapter in <i>Vampire 2e</i> didn't include Bringer-of-Tears, the Rank 4 Get Ahroun<sup>1</sup> - because the werewolves and Lupines of <i>Vampire</i> are not the Garou of <i>Werewolf</i>; they exist as parallel universes more than anything.<br /> <br /> <sup>1-I made this up. It's an example. And also, marketing. </sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:24:38-08:00","id":1052557,"title":"","content":"I have been playing cWoD since 1994 and, at least among the people I played with throughout the USA (from Chicago to NYC to San Diego) it has always been one WoD. Now, no one is saying that anyone has to play crossover games, but it is incorrect to say that it is more than one WoD (there are more than a few dozen of books that explicitly have crossover characters). Just because a specific form of favored supernatural creature does not play well with others does not mean that the others do not exist, it just means that they try to avoid being noticed by the other supernatural entities that can kick their rear end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T09:47:44-08:00","id":1052609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1052433#post1052433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know where you're getting this nebulous &quot;1st edition/2nd edition&quot; divide - there's no clear-cut delineation like there is in something like D&amp;D or Shadowrun, not until the <i>Revised</i> era in 1998 starting with <i>Vampire</i> (and <i>Werewolf</i> and <i>Mage</i> both published in 2000).</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1st and 2nd Editions of the various game lines tend to blur together for a lot of people because of this layered release schedule. I've had several conversation where I've talked exclusively about 1st Edition Vampire, for example, only for people to bring up the contents of the pre-Revised clanbooks as relevant material -- because those are sometimes called the first editions of the clanbooks, as opposed to the Revised versions, even on sites like DriveThruRPG.com. While it's true that they're the first editions of the specific concept of clanbooks, they're still not material for 1st Edition VtM, which, as you correctly note, only ran from 1991 to 1992.<br /> <br /> The terminology we have for the Old/Classic World of Darkness is awkward sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:50:42-08:00","id":1052635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1052557#post1052557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been playing cWoD since 1994 and, at least among the people I played with throughout the USA (from Chicago to NYC to San Diego) it has always been one WoD. Now, no one is saying that anyone has to play crossover games, but it is incorrect to say that it is more than one WoD (there are more than a few dozen of books that explicitly have crossover characters). Just because a specific form of favored supernatural creature does not play well with others does not mean that the others do not exist, it just means that they try to avoid being noticed by the other supernatural entities that can kick their rear end.</div> </div> </div> </div>A hundred people being wrong for 23 years doesn't make it true - this isn't Mage, with its consensual reality. I have repeatedly provided you with literal textual, authorial evidence as to the canonicity of a &quot;Unified WoD,&quot; and its answer in the negative. Just because you don't like the answer doesn't make it any less true. <br /> <br /> Now, the people that want to play and discuss crossover stuff? Go ahead, have a blast - but let's knock it off with this &quot;canon one World of Darkness&quot; nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:08:54-08:00","id":1052641,"title":"","content":"&quot;Vampions&quot; is not necessarily a bad thing. Champions is a great game, although even I wouldn't go so far as to advocate a Champions/WoD crossover...but I have run a WoD/Birthright crossover which my players enjoyed tremendously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:29:46-08:00","id":1052652,"title":"","content":"Definitely not cannon but fitting:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://evildrganymede.net/wp/rpgs/continuum/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://evildrganymede.net/wp/wp-content/uploads/2010/08/contsml.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://evildrganymede.net/wp/rpgs/continuum/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Continuum (oWoD) </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://evildrganymede.net/wp/rpgs/continuum/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://evildrganymede.net/wp/rpgs/continuum/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Continuum is an organisation of Mages outside the Ascension War, dedicated to fighting the Perpetual War against the Darkness (Nephandi/Deep Umbra) that surrounds and seeks to destroy all Reali&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Each splat gets own virtuals.<br /> Problem solved.<br /> For crossover use MC Earth or some other virtual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:29:59-08:00","id":1052729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1052635#post1052635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A hundred people being wrong for 23 years doesn't make it true - this isn't Mage, with its consensual reality. I have repeatedly provided you with literal textual, authorial evidence as to the canonicity of a &amp;quot;Unified WoD,&amp;quot; and its answer in the negative. Just because you don't like the answer doesn't make it any less true. <br /> <br /> Now, the people that want to play and discuss crossover stuff? Go ahead, have a blast - but let's knock it off with this &amp;quot;canon one World of Darkness&amp;quot; nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Midnight Circus? Kindred of the East? Hengeyokai? Pentex: Book of Subsidies? Freak Legion? Ghoul: Fatal Addiction? Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes? Hedge Wizard's Handbook? Ascension's Right Hand? Book of Madness: Revised? Book of the Weaver? Rage Across Russia? Rage Across Appalachia? Rage Across New York? Dream and Nightmares? These are all books that discuss crossover games or give information that supports crossover campaigns. <br /> <br /> Look, it is up to every ST whether or not to decide to run a crossover campaign. Most don't, and that is perfectly fine, but it is one canon cWoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:34:21-08:00","id":1052838,"title":"","content":"And let's not forget official novel lines, like Year of the Scarab and Predator&amp;Prey.<br /> <br /> Calling crossover books rubbish doesn't make those books non-existent or eliminate them as parts of the WoD canon. It's okay to not like them, but they're part of the setting.<br /> <br /> As for Revised curbing back the crossover mayhem of late 2e, that might be true, but you know what was the first place I encountered with Werewolf the Apocalypse? In the antagonist section of the VtM Revised corebook, which said if I'm curious about the side and worldview of werewolves, that is the game about them (I don't have the book at hand right now, so I can't quote the exact line).<br /> <br /> Honestly, my opinion is that crossover was left lousy enough for GMs and writers who don't want(ed) to deal with it for whatever reason (and those reasons are perfectly valid) to be able to say 'nope' to it. WW provided and supported the <i>option</i> for the MWM, but the default was the SWM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:47:03-08:00","id":1052851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1052838#post1052838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And let's not forget official novel lines, like Year of the Scarab and <b>Predator&amp;Prey.</b><br /> <br /> Calling crossover books rubbish doesn't make those books non-existent or eliminate them as parts of the WoD canon. It's okay to not like them, but they're part of the setting.<br /> <br /> As for Revised curbing back the crossover mayhem of late 2e, that might be true, but you know what was the first place I encountered with Werewolf the Apocalypse? In the antagonist section of the VtM Revised corebook, which said if I'm curious about the side and worldview of werewolves, that is the game about them (I don't have the book at hand right now, so I can't quote the exact line).<br /> <br /> Honestly, my opinion is that crossover was left lousy enough for GMs and writers who don't want(ed) to deal with it for whatever reason (and those reasons are perfectly valid) to be able to say 'nope' to it. WW provided and supported the <i>option</i> for the MWM, but the default was the SWM.</div> </div> </div> </div>P&amp;P, wherein a metis Garou knocks up an Imbued woman? That's not a very strong case for actual crossover, as opposed to crossover being painted as ridiculous (even if inadvertently).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:57:06-08:00","id":1052864,"title":"","content":"I'd reiterate: not liking any of the crossover material, or thinking that any particular piece is silly is OK, but that doesn't change the fact that they're the part of official WoD material.<br /> <br /> That a particular novel is not the best novel in the world (although I'm sure there are people out there who enjoyed it) doesn't change that <i>it's an official WoD crossover storyline. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:07:08-08:00","id":1052876,"title":"","content":"Yes, for all we know, it could be a particular weakness of the Imbued which would allow otherwise sterile supernatural entities to knock them up as long as they are sexually functional. After all, it is canon, and it would not change cWoD that much (other than a few unusual pregnancies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T20:29:34-08:00","id":1053014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1052433#post1052433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>All of the rubbish crossover stuff was mid-to-late Second Edition <i>Vampire</i> </b>mostly (excluding the Week of Nightmares and Red Sign stuff, which was rubbish <i>Revised Era</i> stuff, though <i>Blood Treachery</i> (2000) and <i>Ghost Towns</i> (1998) were good).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, so supposing, for argument\u2019s sake, I accept that (false, as noted by Aya Tari) statement, how are the parts of canon you listed non-canonical?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was the <i>Revised Era</i> that said &quot;We're getting too silly. Everyone back to your corners <i>like we were in the beginning</i>.&quot; 1994-98 was the time of &quot;FishMalks&quot; and Sam Haight, when Vampire gained the derogatory label of &quot;vampions,&quot; and Garou were referred to as &quot;Captain Planet wannabees.&quot; </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> P&amp;P, wherein a metis Garou knocks up an Imbued woman? That's not a very strong case for actual crossover, as opposed to crossover being painted as ridiculous (even if inadvertently). </div> </div> </div>I've said it before and I'll say it again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh in the Donald Trump thread</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004230-donald-trump-in-the-wod?p=1007093#post1007093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny how, from time to time, WoD fans and writers will have this horrible realization that some specific WoD trope is silly and they'll get all embarassed and try to abolish that one trope as if that will stop people who turn into wolves and enter the spirit world through mirrors from being silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems that the issue this and many other threads are orbiting is that CWoD fans tend to reserve the right to ignore parts of canon they find silly. Fans have a reached a certain consensus on what qualifies as &quot;silly&quot;, which may be roughly defined as &quot;reminiscent of <u>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</u>, <u>Subsidiaries: a Guide to Pentex</u>, or Sam Haight&quot;. There's a tendency to shoot down any interpretation of canon that meets that definition, or references parts of canon that do.<br /> <br /> I think having a &quot;rule of silly&quot; for your game is in principle completely appropriate and unavoidable when trying to make sense of something as nonsensical as the CWoD. My difficulty is that I find different things silly than most CWoD fans do, and I get frustrated when people who on the whole are cherry-picking just as much as I am shoot down my theories as non-canonical without even acknowledging that they're appealing more to what they find silly than what canon says (which is many contradictory things), much less being willing to discuss what qualifies as silly and why.<br /> <br /> What it looks like to me from the history Nothing gave is that White Wolf wanted to integrate the WoD from the start. The plan was to conceive and design each game separately, so players wouldn\u2019t have to invest in multiple core books, and then gradually merge them once the fans were hooked.<br /> <br /> This didn't work out as well as WW had hoped. Fans reacted poorly to the increase in crossovers. This was partly because fans had become more attached to individual games than to the WoD as a whole, and partly because a lot of the crossovers were just plain badly done and came on too strong.<br /> <br /> This didn't cause WW to give up on crossovers. On the contrary, crossovers continued to be sprinkled throughout Revised, WW just developed a policy of doing them sparingly and leaving interactions and overlaps between the games' metaphysics entirely to the ST. The centerpiece of the Revised metaplot was the Week of Nightmares, a massive crossover metaplot that impacted and involved representatives and metaphysics from every existing gameline, and spawned two new gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5553,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","user":"Mr. Sluagh","date":". 02-21-2017, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T22:02:42-08:00","id":1053041,"title":"","content":"And while we might not like the events of the Week of Nightmares (my 2015 setting has it being avoid by an temporary alliance of Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, Mages, and Wraiths), it is canonical proof that the writers supported one and only one cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T22:08:52-08:00","id":1053045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1053041#post1053041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while we might not like the events of the Week of Nightmares (my 2015 setting has it being avoid by an temporary alliance of Changelings, Fera, Kindred, KJ, Mages, and Wraiths), it is canonical proof that the writers supported one and only one cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I can just as easily say that it's canonical proof that the Worlds occasionally align. <br /> As has been cited, the books make sure to specifically say that the Worlds are different. They never specifically say that they are the same. It is heavily implied in places though.<br /> <br /> So in the end, there are contradictory sources. No one gets too be 100% right, as much as you like to think you know the one true way. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T00:08:57-08:00","id":1053077,"title":"","content":"I'm already as tired of this conversation as I'm sure other people are about reading it; just like I'm tired of feeling like I'm one of the few who owns - much less has read - the <i>Revised Storyteller's Guide</i>, so I'm just going to post the relevant bit here (but I'm also going to hide it behind a spoiler tag, because I'm a jerk like that), so make of it what you will: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Drawing Distinctions,&quot; pages 174-175</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In its design, <b>Vampire</b> is intended to be played as a stand-alone game. The various factions, groups and subcultures prevalent in other games from the Storyteller series quite simply do not exist if you\u2019re playing <b>Vampire</b> exclusively. <b>Vampire</b> has no Silent Striders, no Technocracy and no Unseelie Court <u>as they are defined by the rules</u>.<br /> <br /> <b>This is intentional</b>.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve read the above caveats about the games\u2019 themes degrading when too many disparate elements are introduced. Mages have no Humanity Trait, so mixing them into a coterie of vampires and letting them kill without consequence, while acceptable according to the rules, harms both the mages\u2019 and the vampires\u2019 contribution to the story.<br /> <br /> Certainly, a group of werewolves may <u><i>call</i></u> itself the Silent Striders in your <b>Vampire</b> game, but they\u2019re not going to be the Silent Striders as codified on page whatever of whatever other game line\u2019s book. Vampires aren\u2019t set up to worry about things like Umbras and Shard Realms and the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Now, we\u2019ve been known to break this rule here and there. Necromancy, for example, was rewritten in the revised edition to fit more cleanly with <b>Wraith</b>. These little breaks are considerations for the larger concept. It\u2019s a bit fatuous to have rules for ghosts that, well, fail to take the ghosts into account. But by and large, <b>Vampire</b> doesn\u2019t depend on the presence of other supernaturals. Your coterie has more to worry about with the agitated anarchs than it does from some nebulous and rarely seen motley of changelings (who, by extension, have their own damn problems and don\u2019t give a toss about the vampires...).<br /> <br /> The other supernaturals work better as mysterious allies or enemies, given power by the story\u2019s needs and quantified by the drama the Storyteller wants her troupe to enact. Don\u2019t feel that your city is incomplete because you haven\u2019t created a pack of Bone Gnawers to lurk in the parks and a cult of sluagh to scuttle through the sewers. You don\u2019t need these other elements to play a compelling <b>Vampire</b> game, and 90 percent of the time, you\u2019ll be better off without them. Overpopulating the world with monsters makes the mortals irrelevant \u2014 and if that were the case, vampires would need no Masquerade. The other denizens of the World of Darkness should exist as enigmas rather than reliable staples. Putting aside for a moment the pestilent problem of clan/ tribe/whatever clones, placing a supernatural creature behind every plot makes the Gothic-Punk world far less mysterious. If the Kindred are to fear the fair folk, employing generic redcap hooligans as bouncers in every last one of the city\u2019s nightclubs does the setting and the game a disservice.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re not saying, \u201cDon\u2019t do crossover!\u201d By all means, it\u2019s your game; do what makes you and your players happy. Break the Golden Rule over our collective heads if it entertains you. What we are saying is that you should give consideration to your story\u2019s needs. As Storyteller, you have the most responsibility for making sure the tale you and your troupe tell doesn\u2019t suck. Does the prince\u2019s chauffeur need to be a blood-bound Glass Walker Philodox? Couldn\u2019t he just as easily be a ghoul? Or, even more statistically likely, a normal, oblivious mortal? Familiarity breeds contempt: If the troupe should really fear the bishop\u2019s paid assassin, it\u2019s you\u2019re job to make them quake. You\u2019re just lazy if you rely on them to think, \u201cOh, he\u2019s a werewolf. He can kick our asses.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Gothic-Punk world is ultimately one of subtlety and menace. Ostentation and violence certainly have their place, but consider the logical outcome of any given character\u2019s action. A pistol-wielding gangsta is going to have a short, violent life but is going to get what he wants. The smooth-talking senator\u2019s aide is also going to get it \u2014 and she\u2019s less likely to get whacked in a gang war, arrested for possession, etc. Using the other supernaturals is analagous. If you use them to cow the players or to hurl around strange powers, your game will likely be short and violent. If you use them to build suspense and tension, your game will be longer, richer, deeper and more mature.<br /> <br /> And better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edited for formatting, but emphasis in the original.</div></div> </div> </div>So it seems pretty clear-cut to me. I mean, the first line is &quot;In its design, <i>Vampire</i> is intended to be played as a stand-alone game.&quot;<br /> <br /> And this:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1053014#post1053014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My difficulty is that I find different things silly than most CWoD fans do, and I get frustrated when people who on the whole are cherry-picking just as much as I am shoot down my theories as non-canonical without even acknowledging that they're appealing more to what they find silly than what canon says (which is many contradictory things), much less being willing to discuss what qualifies as silly and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>is a much more interesting conversation - so let's have that one instead.<br /> <br /> Finally, just because I said rubbish doesn't mean I implied non-canonical - it can be canon and poorly done (<i>DSotBH</i> again).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":"paste from a pdf doesn't play well. 02-22-2017, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:50:00-08:00","id":1053205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1053077#post1053077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this:is a much more interesting conversation - so let's have that one instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not at all a fan of &quot;it works because you believe it&quot; and would be able to take Mage much more seriously if instead it was predicated on unknown tracts of reality that weren't subjective, but were just really difficult to see or notice (Edit: and also entirely fictional; it may go over better if the magic has little or nothing to do with real life beliefs). Also, I don't think that putting Dyson spheres into an occult conspiracy setting or the like is very good or original, because comic books did that first and I hadn't assumed that I was playing in DC or Marvel when I picked up the first edition W:tA player's guide and saw the Rokea. So, the further-out scifi elements that Mage introduces with the Technocracy? Also not what I signed up for. I also can't take the &quot;technology is just another type of magic spelled with a k because Crowley&quot;, or Crowley to begin with, for that matter.<br /> <br /> (Advanced prostheses, electromagnetic linear accelerators, and lasers are fine, because we already pretty much have those in real life, but FTL travel and extrasolar colonies with rubber forehead aliens visiting and prisons for Harry Potter types in deep space is right out.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 02-22-2017, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T00:25:09-08:00","id":1055120,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> I agree, actually. I'm a bigger fan of the low-power, street-level stuff - I play <b>Mage</b> closer to <i>Hellblazer</i> than anything, because even things like <i>Dresden Files</i> are too over-the-top, in my opinion. I mean, I can see the appeal for others, but I think <b>Mage Revised</b> was the best version of the game, and mostly because the Avatar Storm scoured away a lot of that extra-crazy stuff.<br /> <br /> <i>Dirty Secrets...</i> gets a lot of flak, but it introduced the True Brujah, who I find really interesting as an organization (and I'm a sucker for time-manipulation stuff).<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 02-26-2017, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T01:04:34-08:00","id":1055126,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to make a remark about 'canon' for the WoD.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere have been so many developers and authors involved that I promise you, there are plenty of references both ways, sometimes from the same people.<br /> <br /> You've got the Revised Players Guide, then you have 2 Mage/Vampire crossovers right after, and a Revenant Family that is tied to the Shadow Lords in the Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> What people are looking for in crossover books seemed to me to be:<br /> <br /> \u200b1) Story hooks to engage PCs on multiple angles.<br /> \u200b2) How to handle conflicting stat checks and discrepancies. The most obvious is Humanity/Virtues, but others do exist. IE: A Pooka, a Verbena, and a Gangrel turn into a Wolf. The Garou gets much more awesome stats for it.<br /> \u200b3) Why are the villains all able to work together, but not the 'heroes'? As I've brought up in another thread, there are repeated references to Sabbat working with Nephandi and BSDs, despite routing out Infernalism in their own ranks, and wanting to kill ancient monsters so they can't eat the world, while the latter wants to wake them up and help them. That sounds like a conflict of interest that 'respecting monsters who aren't trying to be human' isn't going to cover.<br /> \u200b4) Mobility issues. (most games I've been in have already dismissed the 'avatar storm' as being heavy handed, though keep most of the huge umbra installations as gone, though more from infighting than from WtA umbrood doing it.) Blood Dimmed Tides was actually fairly successful at showing how a variety of creatures could have aquatic adventures.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhile you have some sources that can be helpful, some just aren't. And some boiled down to &quot;Splat X wins, crossovers suck, case closed, stop asking.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bThe response comes from cosmology, which I never understood why it was a huge issue. From a Mage point of view, X is true. From a shapechanger's point of view, y is true. It doesn't mean either is false. Especially when you can also say the same about two different Mages (in fact, it's a major point of the game) or two different shapechangers (though to a lesser degree).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5818,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","user":"EvilTyger","date":". 02-26-2017, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T11:40:44-08:00","id":1055326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055120#post1055120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> I agree, actually. I'm a bigger fan of the low-power, street-level stuff - I play <b>Mage</b> closer to <i>Hellblazer</i> than anything, because even things like <i>Dresden Files</i> are too over-the-top, in my opinion. I mean, I can see the appeal for others, but I think <b>Mage Revised</b> was the best version of the game, and mostly because the Avatar Storm scoured away a lot of that extra-crazy stuff.<br /> <br /> <i>Dirty Secrets...</i> gets a lot of flak, but it introduced the True Brujah, who I find really interesting as an organization (and I'm a sucker for time-manipulation stuff).<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't have been so bad if everyone had been on the same page, so that no one got left behind. But everything is far away, now. So very far. And with no forewarning in any book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b1) Story hooks to engage PCs on multiple angles.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b2) How to handle conflicting stat checks and discrepancies. The most obvious is Humanity/Virtues, but others do exist. IE: A Pooka, a Verbena, and a Gangrel turn into a Wolf. The Garou gets much more awesome stats for it.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Actually, Werewolf: the Dark Ages (not to be confused with Dark Ages: Werewolf) and KotE had some suggestions in that area that were far from unreasonable. It always seems to come down to some Vampire enthusiasts throwing a tantrum because said pooka and werewolves might (gasp!) have higher effective Courage ratings and not urinate themselves when presented with Presence 5 or the like.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b3) Why are the villains all able to work together, but not the 'heroes'? As I've brought up in another thread, there are repeated references to Sabbat working with Nephandi and BSDs, despite routing out Infernalism in their own ranks, and wanting to kill ancient monsters so they can't eat the world, while the latter wants to wake them up and help them. That sounds like a conflict of interest that 'respecting monsters who aren't trying to be human' isn't going to cover.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's pretty much a dual issue of early installment weirdness and opposition that has a very tenuous method of cooperation. Presumably, some on the other side of this have stabler and easier arrangements, such as Rokea and merfolk, or Jade Kingdom wraiths and Wu Lung descended from their familial lines.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b4) Mobility issues. (most games I've been in have already dismissed the 'avatar storm' as being heavy handed, though keep most of the huge umbra installations as gone, though more from infighting than from WtA umbrood doing it.) Blood Dimmed Tides was actually fairly successful at showing how a variety of creatures could have aquatic adventures.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Though, in line with my response to #3, some underwater splats won't get along, like Gangrel mariners or Lasombra pirates and pretty much anything else but maritime ghosts and possibly merdhuacha.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bWhile you have some sources that can be helpful, some just aren't. And some boiled down to &quot;Splat X wins, crossovers suck, case closed, stop asking.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThe response comes from cosmology, which I never understood why it was a huge issue. From a Mage point of view, X is true. From a shapechanger's point of view, y is true. It doesn't mean either is false. Especially when you can also say the same about two different Mages (in fact, it's a major point of the game) or two different shapechangers (though to a lesser degree).</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Mage has an extremely particular way of looking at Creation that often puts a serious cramp on other games because it often boils down to &quot;so which one of you mother fuckers didn't <i>believe</i> hard enough?&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 02-26-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T01:20:11-08:00","id":1055561,"title":"","content":"I have a thought experiment that may yield some insight into what I believe to be the crux of the issue being discussed here. And here it is:<br /> <br /> Four people each come into possession of a copy of Werewolf: the Apocalypse. Each one lives in a remote part of the world where there's little internet connectivity, and there is only one small hobby store in town that only has a smattering of second hand copies of tabletop roleplaying games at best. Never the less, these four people love the hobby and quickly World of Darkness becomes their favorit tabletop game to run with their friends. They all run many Werewolf Chronicles with their respected gaming groups, and it becomes a very important part of the four individual's lives. However, each of the four individuals have a different version of Werewolf: the Apocolypse (1st Edition, 2nd Edition, Revised Edition, and the 20th Anniversary Edition), and by some cosmic chance each never discovers any other version beyond the ones they already own. The question then is this: does each of these four individual's Chronicles take place in the same World of Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 02-27-2017, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T07:19:20-08:00","id":1055640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055561#post1055561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a thought experiment that may yield some insight into what I believe to be the crux of the issue being discussed here. And here it is:<br /> <br /> Four people each come into possession of a copy of Werewolf: the Apocalypse. Each one lives in a remote part of the world where there's little internet connectivity, and there is only one small hobby store in town that only has a smattering of second hand copies of tabletop roleplaying games at best. Never the less, these four people love the hobby and quickly World of Darkness becomes their favorit tabletop game to run with their friends. They all run many Werewolf Chronicles with their respected gaming groups, and it becomes a very important part of the four individual's lives. However, each of the four individuals have a different version of Werewolf: the Apocolypse (1st Edition, 2nd Edition, Revised Edition, and the 20th Anniversary Edition), and by some cosmic chance each never discovers any other version beyond the ones they already own. The question then is this: does each of these four individual's Chronicles take place in the same World of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, even setting aside crossover or metaplot, they'll all be rather strikingly different. The first three have differences between editions that are never actually made into metaplot elements, like the mirror requirements to step sideways being made into mere suggestions in Revised, and in presentation of certain elements (compare the original Fianna and Get of Fenris tribebooks to their far better-considered and -researched Revised-era counterparts), while W20 removes some more baggage in presentation (Pure Breed no longer has anything to do with human ethnic heritage, for one) but also changes around some cosmology, as the &quot;High Umbra&quot; or Astral Umbra used to be a subset of the Deep Umbra in past W:tA editions, and finally correct Revised's habitual misspelling/misRomanization of the Boli Zousizhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T12:48:31-08:00","id":1055748,"title":"","content":"Well, for those that are STILL saying that nonsense about &quot;cannonical one WoD&quot;.<br /> <br /> For the WtA players, are you ready to agree that all of the Gaia talk is a HUGE bullshit? Are you all ready to acknowledge the Lore from Demon as the one and only ultimate truth of the One WoD? Well, possibily, it was Lucifer all along that you guys were fighting for...<br /> <br /> As for the Mage players, are you ready to acknowledge that all that talk about Avatars, and Consensus and Subjective Reality is all bullshit? Are you all ready to acknowledge that your precious avatars are just the corpses of the dead angels of the great war on demon the fallen?<br /> <br /> As for Vampire players... It's all cool. Yep, Cain killed Abel and were turned by God himself into the 1th generation vamp. Well done guys.<br /> <br /> Well, if you all feel confortable with this, by all means, lets call it &quot;cannon One WoD&quot;. Have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T13:15:37-08:00","id":1055754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055126#post1055126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b3) Why are the villains all able to work together, but not the 'heroes'? As I've brought up in another thread, there are repeated references to Sabbat working with Nephandi and BSDs, despite routing out Infernalism in their own ranks, and wanting to kill ancient monsters so they can't eat the world, while the latter wants to wake them up and help them. That sounds like a conflict of interest that 'respecting monsters who aren't trying to be human' isn't going to cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I ALWAYS say:<br /> <br /> WHY DA FUC DONT THE DAMN CHANGELLINGS (previous Fae) UNITE WITH THE TRADITIONS AGAINST THE TECHNOCRACY? ARE THEY BLIND?<br /> <br /> Really, to assume a unique WoD is more than absurd and preposterous. Why da hell haven't an alliance between tribes like Children of Gaia and Fianna haven't been made with Dreamspeakers, Verbena and the Seelie Court?<br /> <br /> And, how could you play WtA without EVER facing one HIT MARK from the Union?<br /> <br /> How could you play with a member of the Syndicate and NEVER become targeted by the Giovanni?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:52:50-08:00","id":1055804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055126#post1055126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to make a remark about 'canon' for the WoD.<br /> <br /> \u200b3) Why are the villains all able to work together, but not the 'heroes'? As I've brought up in another thread, there are repeated references to Sabbat working with Nephandi and BSDs, despite routing out Infernalism in their own ranks, and wanting to kill ancient monsters so they can't eat the world, while the latter wants to wake them up and help them. That sounds like a conflict of interest that 'respecting monsters who aren't trying to be human' isn't going to cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those references are either from the more crossover-heavy 2nd edition and/or passing mentions in non-Vampire books. I'm sure there are individual instances of Sabbat packs teaming up BSD's and Nephandi, but it's not as if there's some secret Legion of Doom meeting where the Prisci Council meets up with a bunch of BSDs and Nephandi to plot teh evilz. Honestly in most of the Sabbat games I've played its not been uncommon for BSDs and Nephandi to be antagonists. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055754#post1055754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I ALWAYS say:<br /> <br /> WHY DA FUC DONT THE DAMN CHANGELLINGS (previous Fae) UNITE WITH THE TRADITIONS AGAINST THE TECHNOCRACY? ARE THEY BLIND?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for the most part Changelings are beneath the Technocracy's notice and therefore the Technocracy doesn't really go out of its way to fuck with Changelings. The Kithain don't have any particular reason to know about or even care about the Technocracy beyond a broad philosophical imperative, which considering the threat's remoteness is going to seem pretty insignificant next to whatever pressing Changeling shit they're dealing with at that moment. Additionally, Mages are dicks. Its kinda their thing. Whatever they may have in common its pretty much inevitable that Changeling/Mage interaction will end with Mages sticking their magickal dicks into places they don't belong and generally being condescending to everyone involved. The Kithain aren't presented with any particularly compelling reason to ally with Mages against the threat they don't have any compelling reason to care about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:26:11-08:00","id":1055831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055748#post1055748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the WtA players, are you ready to agree that all of the Gaia talk is a HUGE bullshit? Are you all ready to acknowledge the Lore from Demon as the one and only ultimate truth of the One WoD? Well, possibily, it was Lucifer all along that you guys were fighting for...<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis conversation actually happened IC between a demon and another character in one of the games I was in. The response:<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;So you are telling me you've been around since Creation, but buried under a few billion dead human souls, locked up where the total of human misery has seeped in, and have to spiritually bind yourself to a human in order to stay out, and think it has had no effect on either your memory, or your perceptions of reality? &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:44:26-08:00","id":1055872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055831#post1055831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThis conversation actually happened IC between a demon and another character in one of the games I was in. The response:<br /> <br /> \u200b&amp;quot;So you are telling me you've been around since Creation, but buried under a few billion dead human souls, locked up where the total of human misery has seeped in, and have to spiritually bind yourself to a human in order to stay out, and think it has had no effect on either your memory, or your perceptions of reality? &amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter, you may say that in game, and it is cool to say it. But, when (if) they print the &quot;One WoD&quot;, it will be the world of Jeovah, with Lucifer and stuff. Honestly, I think it is far cooler to say &quot;hey fallen dude, you're high bro&quot;, but the fact remains that the idea of WoD has been the world of God (or &quot;The One&quot; if you prefer) since day 1. Which is why Vampire, the first game EVER of WoD IS, in fact, the world of God (with all the biblical Caim and stuff, something that I always hated by the way, the reason being EXACTLY because I don't like &quot;God&quot; being the Creator of WoD)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:18:53-08:00","id":1055891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055872#post1055872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't matter, you may say that in game, and it is cool to say it. But, when (if) they print the &quot;One WoD&quot;, it will be the world of Jeovah, with Lucifer and stuff. Honestly, I think it is far cooler to say &quot;hey fallen dude, you're high bro&quot;, but the fact remains that the idea of WoD has been the world of God (or &quot;The One&quot; if you prefer) since day 1. Which is why Vampire, the first game EVER of WoD IS, in fact, the world of God (with all the biblical Caim and stuff, something that I always hated by the way, the reason being EXACTLY because I don't like &quot;God&quot; being the Creator of WoD)</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite the fact that it reinforces Vampire lore over any of the other game lines I actually kinda hate Demon lore. I get as grumpy as the next guy when Vampire cosmology is trivialized by other game lines, but Demon is like a condescending blunt instrument. I think a big part of Demon's problem is that it while it ostensibly carves out a Vampire friendly cosmology they don't really work together because Demon falls into the same trap that a lot of the other game lines do: it makes Demons the heroes. Not that they are &quot;heroic,&quot; but they are unquestionably the heroes in that the game casts them as capital 'P' Protagonists in a great apocalyptic struggle with universal stakes. Their actions <i>matter</i> and they know it. Vampire is about being inconsequential. Whether you're a thin-blooded Neonate or a Methuseleh you are trapped in a horrifying game with neither rules nor a victor whose outcome is wholly meaningless. Even its looming end times are never really portrayed as a thing that can be triumphed over or even survived, its just kind of a ticking clock until everything dies in a spasm of violence and futility. Its outlook is more than anything else what makes it inimitable to many other game lines, of which Demon is one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T20:42:52-08:00","id":1055967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055891#post1055891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite the fact that it reinforces Vampire lore over any of the other game lines I actually kinda hate Demon lore. I get as grumpy as the next guy when Vampire cosmology is trivialized by other game lines, but Demon is like a condescending blunt instrument. I think a big part of Demon's problem is that it while it ostensibly carves out a Vampire friendly cosmology they don't really work together because Demon falls into the same trap that a lot of the other game lines do: it makes Demons the heroes. Not that they are &amp;quot;heroic,&amp;quot; but they are unquestionably the heroes in that the game casts them as capital 'P' Protagonists in a great apocalyptic struggle with universal stakes. Their actions <i>matter</i> and they know it. Vampire is about being inconsequential. Whether you're a thin-blooded Neonate or a Methuseleh you are trapped in a horrifying game with neither rules nor a victor whose outcome is wholly meaningless. Even its looming end times are never really portrayed as a thing that can be triumphed over or even survived, its just kind of a ticking clock until everything dies in a spasm of violence and futility. Its outlook is more than anything else what makes it inimitable to many other game lines, of which Demon is one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the only other game with the same level of despair (or more) is wraith.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there is no way to bound the many different games of WoD into one only, not without trashing several of the lines. What I saw many guys here who are mainly fans of WtA pose as a &quot;solution&quot; is to put everything under the rule of the Triat, and Gaia above all...<br /> <br /> So, vampires are the descendants of some crazy High Umbra spirits, humans Avatars of Mages are gaian spirits who lost their purpose and were &quot;magnetized&quot; towards humans, Changellings are creatures from one of the Realms of the Wyld, and Demons are spirits of the Wyrm trapped on Abyss/Oblivion and who lost their memories and purpose because of that.<br /> <br /> And that's all a HUGE piece of poo.<br /> <br /> We might as well go with Changelling &quot;Werewolves and the other werefreaks are lost kiths... They are dreams who forgot who they are&quot;, and be equally shit. Or go with &quot; werewolves? Bah, some millions of wolf spirits started dreaming about being humans, and they wanted that so much that they shifted Consensus!&quot; (funny enough, that may be the least shit. For werewolves at least. But it will still be very shit for vampires and demons - at least, demons as it is; Umbrood mischievous spirits would do just fine under Consensus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T20:53:03-08:00","id":1055973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055872#post1055872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't matter, you may say that in game, and it is cool to say it. But, when (if) they print the &quot;One WoD&quot;, it will be the world of Jeovah, with Lucifer and stuff. Honestly, I think it is far cooler to say &quot;hey fallen dude, you're high bro&quot;, but the fact remains that the idea of WoD has been the world of God (or &quot;The One&quot; if you prefer) since day 1. Which is why Vampire, the first game EVER of WoD IS, in fact, the world of God (with all the biblical Caim and stuff, something that I always hated by the way, the reason being EXACTLY because I don't like &quot;God&quot; being the Creator of WoD)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Ugebzq3juE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Ugebzq3juE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Ugebzq3juE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Ugebzq3juE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T00:46:35-08:00","id":1056011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055561#post1055561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a thought experiment that may yield some insight into what I believe to be the crux of the issue being discussed here. And here it is:<br /> <br /> Four people each come into possession of a copy of Werewolf: the Apocalypse. Each one lives in a remote part of the world where there's little internet connectivity, and there is only one small hobby store in town that only has a smattering of second hand copies of tabletop roleplaying games at best. Never the less, these four people love the hobby and quickly World of Darkness becomes their favorit tabletop game to run with their friends. They all run many Werewolf Chronicles with their respected gaming groups, and it becomes a very important part of the four individual's lives. However, each of the four individuals have a different version of Werewolf: the Apocolypse (1st Edition, 2nd Edition, Revised Edition, and the 20th Anniversary Edition), and by some cosmic chance each never discovers any other version beyond the ones they already own. The question then is this: does each of these four individual's Chronicles take place in the same World of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I'd go as far as to say that if you have people that you described, and that they all happened to get the same edition of Werewolf, they'd still be playing games do drastically different they may as well be set in completley different Worlds of Darkness.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T01:00:53-08:00","id":1056015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1055967#post1055967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, there is no way to bound the many different games of WoD into one only, not without trashing several of the lines. What I saw many guys here who are mainly fans of WtA pose as a &quot;solution&quot; is to put everything under the rule of the Triat, and Gaia above all...<br /> <br /> So, vampires are the descendants of some crazy High Umbra spirits, humans Avatars of Mages are gaian spirits who lost their purpose and were &quot;magnetized&quot; towards humans, Changellings are creatures from one of the Realms of the Wyld, and Demons are spirits of the Wyrm trapped on Abyss/Oblivion and who lost their memories and purpose because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's much simpler then that. At one point when monotheism was starting in human history it spawned a new facet of the Weaver known as the Patriarch. The Patriarch is the emobidiement of &quot;God Father&quot; as pursued by monotheistic Faiths. It is a being of Order and ritual, and it has feasted on the collective chiminage of humanity through the ages. It was more then powerful enough to punish one of its early adherents with a Curse for daring to slay its own brother and chosen priest...<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(n.b. The Patriarch is an easy shoe in, but with how Umbra, chiminage, Faith and prayer work, you could easily have an Incarna level spirit formed or feeding from the collective monotheistic Faiths)</span><br /> <br /> Or maybe it was the Eater of Souls who descended upon a man who murdered his brother, driven mad by his deed and created a once in a lifetime marriage of flesh and debases spirit, making a special kind of fomor that could breed true...<br /> <br /> <br /> I have no idea where your interpretations of what Mages, Changelings and Demons are came from, but they are batshit insane and not related to anything actually said in the Werewolf books. If you have to shoehorn things into a cosmology at least research it a bit to see what might be plausible within it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T01:11:35-08:00","id":1056017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056015#post1056015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) It was more then powerful enough to punish one of its early adherents with a Curse for daring to slay its own brother and chosen priest...<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(n.b. The Patriarch is an easy shoe in, but with how Umbra, chiminage, Faith and prayer work, you could easily have an Incarna level spirit formed or feeding from the collective monotheistic Faiths)</span><br /> <br /> Or maybe it was the Eater of Souls who descended upon a man who murdered his brother, driven mad by his deed and created a once in a lifetime marriage of flesh and debases spirit, making a special kind of fomor that could breed true...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It could have been both - the Patriarch punished, while the Eater-of-Souls saw an opportunity to make of the punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T04:06:41-08:00","id":1056048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056015#post1056015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it's much simpler then that. At one point when monotheism was starting in human history it spawned a new facet of the Weaver known as the Patriarch. The Patriarch is the emobidiement of &amp;quot;God Father&amp;quot; as pursued by monotheistic Faiths. It is a being of Order and ritual, and it has feasted on the collective chiminage of humanity through the ages. It was more then powerful enough to punish one of its early adherents with a Curse for daring to slay its own brother and chosen priest...<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(n.b. The Patriarch is an easy shoe in, but with how Umbra, chiminage, Faith and prayer work, you could easily have an Incarna level spirit formed or feeding from the collective monotheistic Faiths)</span><br /> <br /> Or maybe it was the Eater of Souls who descended upon a man who murdered his brother, driven mad by his deed and created a once in a lifetime marriage of flesh and debases spirit, making a special kind of fomor that could breed true...<br /> <br /> <br /> I have no idea where your interpretations of what Mages, Changelings and Demons are came from, but they are batshit insane and not related to anything actually said in the Werewolf books. If you have to shoehorn things into a cosmology at least research it a bit to see what might be plausible within it.</div> </div> </div> </div>See? That's what I mean. A load of poo.<br /> <br /> Please, keep your simplistic cosmology with your WtA games. This is total, absolute trash for ANY other splats.<br /> <br /> About where I took my ideas for the other splats, those aren't mine, they are ideas of WtA players posted on the forum throghout many different threads. So, go tell them to do their research (such a condescending tone, like if I didnt know that game well enough, just as much as any of the other splats). And it doesn't matter, it's just examples of how shitty such solutions are, it could've been any other attempts, it would still be a load of crap, no matter from what lenses you look at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T04:09:08-08:00","id":1056049,"title":"","content":"&quot;Fomorian vampires&quot;, thats a game I would like to play - like, never in my life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T04:55:48-08:00","id":1056059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056048#post1056048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About where I took my ideas for the other splats, those aren't mine, they are ideas of WtA players posted on the forum throghout many different threads. So, go tell them to do their research (such a condescending tone, like if I didnt know that game well enough, just as much as any of the other splats). And it doesn't matter, it's just examples of how shitty such solutions are, it could've been any other attempts, it would still be a load of crap, no matter from what lenses you look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werwolf itself doesn't go into exact details. Because it does not matter. For the average Werewolf game,Vampires are a non issue or a minor antagonist at best. They are not relevant. Even when they are they are vampires entirely designed to fulfil the narrative niche within Werewolf. Like say the Setites, that are turned into a debased evil version of Set from the Conan cartoon and who gain powers that completely have nothing to do with Disciplines.<br /> <br /> You're the one pulling out random descriptions without actually understanding how Werewolf works. Since you are deeply affronted by people misrepresenting and disagreeing with the Vampire/Demon partyline, you should at least be able to realise that some of us might not agree with such an alien perspective. But at least we can be civil about it. You should too.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":".  Removed nitpick about fomori and fomorians 02-28-2017, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T05:29:45-08:00","id":1056066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056059#post1056059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werwolf itself doesn't go into exact details. Because it does not matter. For the average Werewolf game,Vampires are a non issue or a minor antagonist at best. They are not relevant. Even when they are they are vampires entirely designed to fulfil the narrative niche within Werewolf. Like say the Setites, that are turned into a debased evil version of Set from the Conan cartoon and who gain powers that completely have nothing to do with Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's EXACTLY my point. Thank you for agreeing with me. Those games don't mix. Yes, you're ABSOLUTELY right, vampires DONT MATTER on a werewolf game. And neither does Mages or changellings. Likewise, werewolves are just a minor &quot;weirdness&quot; on a mage game, or a simple plot device for a Vampire game... There will be no Garou Nation at war with the local Pentex, just &quot;they say the Wolves are in the farm Jimmy. That's why the Prince wont send personal there&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thank you, I rest my case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056059#post1056059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're the one pulling out random descriptions without actually understanding how Werewolf works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahn... No, I'm not. Like I said, those were all (non Cannon of course) ideas from wereolf's players, not mine, all posted along several different places of this f\u00f3rum, but they are all here. And, to be honest, it's just random examples, I never said that &quot;that's in the books&quot;. However, they are fitting examples of how WtA would work, and shitty that would be for other splats (but not just from WtA, just try to put your triat under the Consensus of Mage)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056059#post1056059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you are deeply affronted by people misrepresenting and disagreeing with the Vampire/Demon partyline, you should at least be able to realise that some of us might not agree with such an alien perspective. But at least we can be civil about it. You should too.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Civil? Im not the one calling you ignorant and telling you to &quot;do your homework&quot; and go research things before (saying shit).<br /> <br /> However, that's EXACTLY what you told me... Using prettier words, but it's that.<br /> <br /> I don't care about Vampire/Demon lore/cosmology. Thats the thing. I'm perfectly confortable with considering Vampires as humans infected by some weird Paradox, for example, if we go with Mage, or to call Demons of just some High Umbrood spirits. Just as much as I don't care for &quot;technology is Weaver&quot; on a WtA game, and not the byproduct of Consensus.<br /> <br /> But<br /> <br /> As you state ABOVE<br /> <br /> I WONT play Mage having technology as &quot;Weaver&quot;, rather than technocratic Consensus. And, I wont play Vampire as a creation of the Eater of Souls. No more than I would play Werewolf as some deluded Lucifer's pawns.<br /> <br /> Im not affronted by misrepresenting Vampires, or demons, or Mages or whatever in another game.<br /> <br /> But you DO seem affronted to see that werewolf lore just isn't fit OR useful for other splats, and you DO seem affronted by seem it misrepresented on other games. My only question is: why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T05:36:22-08:00","id":1056068,"title":"","content":"So, my point is: Vampires, as the progeny of the Eater of Souls or of a big Patriarch Incarnae, is great for a WtA game.<br /> <br /> But it sucks for VtM.<br /> <br /> Or, would you play a game of WtA were ALL Fera are just some Paradox Spirits? (Hey, that's actually not a bad one for mage)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T05:39:06-08:00","id":1056071,"title":"","content":"Likewise, Mage without Consensus isn't Mage. It would be like Vampire without Jyhad, Werewolf without Gaia, Changelling without Banality and Wraith without Oblivion (like has already been discussed on another thread)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T06:14:50-08:00","id":1056082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056068#post1056068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my point is: Vampires, as the progeny of the Eater of Souls or of a big Patriarch Incarnae, is great for a WtA game.<br /> <br /> But it sucks for VtM.<br /> <br /> Or, would you play a game of WtA were ALL Fera are just some Paradox Spirits? (Hey, that's actually not a bad one for mage)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWerewolves believing (or more accurately, hypothesizing) that that may be the case doesn't make it objectively true. (And in fact, werewolves never claim it to be an object truth, more of a warning fairy tale like the Brother's Grim.)<br /> <br /> In fact, WtA goes out of its way to show that the Garou Nation has made many, many mistakes over the course of the millennia.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe only ones that MIGHT know what happened are the demons, and my earlier post in this thread, has it's own reasons to take with a grain of salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:38:42-08:00","id":1056105,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> Wow. So where did I advocate any of these points? I'm just protesting a rather bizarre description you posited about how the splats would work in Werewolf. I've never said anything about this opic in this thread before this. And looking at the rest of this thread you're mostly arguing with yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:10:38-08:00","id":1056120,"title":"","content":"I do not think that anyone is arguing against the Consensus, just what the Consensus effects. In crossovers, it pretty much only effects Mages and their creations (otherwise it is just a Mage game with superfriends).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:08:35-08:00","id":1056223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056048#post1056048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See? That's what I mean. A load of poo.<br /> <br /> Please, keep your simplistic cosmology with your WtA games. This is total, absolute trash for ANY other splats.<br /> <br /> About where I took my ideas for the other splats, those aren't mine, they are ideas of WtA players posted on the forum throghout many different threads. So, go tell them to do their research (such a condescending tone, like if I didnt know that game well enough, just as much as any of the other splats). And it doesn't matter, it's just examples of how shitty such solutions are, it could've been any other attempts, it would still be a load of crap, no matter from what lenses you look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, while I'm mostly agreeing with you here I feel like I need to politely ask you to dial it back. You're not doing any favors for your side (which I am for the most part on) with your persistently combative tone. Its a game guys, lets be chill. <br /> <br /> For my own two cents, I've also always been pretty miffed at the &quot;Vampires are Fomori&quot; stance. I like Fomori, but lumping an entire game splat into a broad subsplat of another game is pretty reductive. If Vampires are Wyrmspawn can't they at least warrant their own special variety?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:22:05-08:00","id":1056269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056066#post1056066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a bunch of caustic stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like someone isn't happy with their place in the food chain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-28-2017, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:28:38-08:00","id":1056275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056269#post1056269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like someone isn't happy with their place in the food chain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude. Come on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:36:35-08:00","id":1056302,"title":"","content":"It's every damn thread. I don't know why you mollycoddle him.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T14:15:13-08:00","id":1056317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056302#post1056302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's every damn thread. I don't know why you mollycoddle him.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't actually particularly give a shit about him, but that whole food chain bullshit burns my buns just as much as it does his. Its part of an overall attitude that is equally unproductive to the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T15:55:32-08:00","id":1056356,"title":"","content":"But there is literally a food chain in cWoD. Kindred and KJ feed on mortals, as do Ananasi Fera, Kithain Changelings, Wraiths, etc. Mages figuratively feed on mortals by sacrificing them for their version of the Concensus. Gaian Fera do not tend to feed on mortals, though there are nasty exceptions.<br /> <br /> When it comes to beginning characters from the classic five gamelines, there is a pecking order. Ajaba, Bastet, Garou, Gurahl, Mokole, Nagah, and Rokea are the most powerful beginning characters. Ananasi, Corax, Kindred, Kitsune, KJ, Nuwushi, and Ratkin are the next most powerful beginning characters. Changelings and Mages are the second least powerful beginning characters. Wraiths are the least powerful beginning characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T17:15:16-08:00","id":1056382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056269#post1056269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like someone isn't happy with their place in the food chain.</div> </div> </div> </div>LMAO \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02 LMAO","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T17:21:05-08:00","id":1056384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056082#post1056082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWerewolves believing (or more accurately, hypothesizing) that that may be the case doesn't make it objectively true. (And in fact, werewolves never claim it to be an object truth, more of a warning fairy tale like the Brother's Grim.)<br /> <br /> In fact, WtA goes out of its way to show that the Garou Nation has made many, many mistakes over the course of the millennia.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe only ones that MIGHT know what happened are the demons, and my earlier post in this thread, has it's own reasons to take with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, crossovers will work as long as you don't need to deal with the conflicts. Let the demons say they waged war against God, let Garou talk about Gaia and Mage tell you how the men in Black shape reality. As long as you don't have to deal with those matters, it will not be a problem. But, when you DO need to change the faiths of an entire city, you'll have problems...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T18:21:12-08:00","id":1056404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056120#post1056120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that anyone is arguing against the Consensus, just what the Consensus effects. In crossovers, it pretty much only effects Mages and their creations (otherwise it is just a Mage game with superfriends).</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said on the other crossover thread, some people are just hell-bent on picking one gameline's mythology as &quot;truth&quot;. I never got that, for me they're compatible and became incompatible just in the case of taking them to the extreme. Vampire's God can be many things that could fit into the other line's worldview. The consensus could work with the other lines if approaching it with the earthly foundations and mythic threads in mind.<br /> <br /> Same with the organizations.<br /> <br /> Honestly, having as many crossover elements as we have, crossover is canon to me, period. Constantly saying that &quot;oooh, but the critters in this book (even when that book is intentionally a crossover book) aren't the critters from the other game, really&quot; is getting old after a point. That the authors themselves had varied opinions on crossovers, I'm okay with that and with thematic purity (although sometimes it's starting to look as &quot;get off from my lawn&quot; joke), but honestly, it's also somewhat lazy referring to that again and again instead of writing more compatible rules and taking into mind the other games when writing a supplement, with more interactions between the splats, etc.<br /> <br /> I might have been read too much urban fantasy, but in my mind it's always better to having a diverse setting with multiple splats (with the possibility of focusing on just one if I want) than an entirely &quot;purist&quot; setting and honestly, WoD started that whole genre back in the day. As far as I'm aware, WoD was the first setting with vamps, (multiple) werecreatures, fairies, mages, etc. in it that countless authors copied afterward to some extent.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T23:01:21-08:00","id":1056495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056404#post1056404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I said on the other crossover thread, some people are just hell-bent on picking one gameline's mythology as &quot;truth&quot;. I never got that, for me they're compatible and became incompatible just in the case of taking them to the extreme. Vampire's God can be many things that could fit into the other line's worldview. The consensus could work with the other lines if approaching it with the earthly foundations and mythic threads in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>The consensus will definitely not work for Werewolf. Exactly why has been repeated many, many times. The moment you introduce consensus and subjective reality, W:tA leaves the building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:34:51-08:00","id":1056522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056356#post1056356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is literally a food chain in cWoD. Kindred and KJ feed on mortals, as do Ananasi Fera, Kithain Changelings, Wraiths, etc. Mages figuratively feed on mortals by sacrificing them for their version of the Concensus. Gaian Fera do not tend to feed on mortals, though there are nasty exceptions.<br /> <br /> When it comes to beginning characters from the classic five gamelines, there is a pecking order. Ajaba, Bastet, Garou, Gurahl, Mokole, Nagah, and Rokea are the most powerful beginning characters. Ananasi, Corax, Kindred, Kitsune, KJ, Nuwushi, and Ratkin are the next most powerful beginning characters. Changelings and Mages are the second least powerful beginning characters. Wraiths are the least powerful beginning characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is really simplistic, but more importantly, it's an incredibly tedious topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T01:43:50-08:00","id":1056534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056495#post1056495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The consensus will definitely not work for Werewolf. Exactly why has been repeated many, many times. The moment you introduce consensus and subjective reality, W:tA leaves the building.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. That is my point, I have to repeat it all the time. There are a few points of conflict between all games, but none like Werewolf and Mage. They are water and oil, period. The werewolves in a Mage game are NOT properly Garou, and the Mages in a Werewolf game are NOT the awakened. Period.<br /> <br /> And I don't understand why is that a problem. They are different games, why does that bother s\u00f3 many people? <br /> <br /> And it's not just the cosmology that is incompatible; I gotta say, mage is THE MOST incompatible game of all. It's not just the Consensus; Mage also have the.Technocracy, WoD big trouble boy. Problem is, Mage only works with a huge, &quot;all&quot; powerful Technocracy that kick ass all around... In theory, althouth they aren't in every world's toilets watching everybody poo, but they are kicking some supernatural butts since they arrived. The Technocracy won't work as just some vampire-mortal inquisition-minor antagonist sort of organization. It simply won't. Problem is, other splats simply won't work with the ever watchful eye of the big brothers. <br /> <br /> You can of course make some EXCUSES to poorly fit everything togheter. Like saying &quot;oh, vampires keep to their own&quot;, or &quot;why would changellings work with Mages?&quot; and &quot;Charon forbids wraiths to interact with the living&quot;. But the thruth is, the Dreamspeakers would NEVER be part of the Traditions, they would, much more likely, become an unique kind of kinfolk faction, allying with the Garou nation (that's something that the spirits themselves would ask to both factions possible). It's also possible that the Verbena would do the same. The Traditions would ally with the Seelie Court, after proving to the Changellings that &quot;this conspiracy called the Union of the Technocratic Conventions are the guys bringing your dreaded banality and hunting you... Help us to help you&quot;. Alliances and skirmishes with local vampires would be all too common, since the kindred would try to use other critters as pawns in their games or would see them as threaths; so, at least SOME kindred politics would be a common theme on all the nightfolks mouths. And the Technocracy would be out there, trying to hit everybody and everything at once all the time, probably being spinned around by the methuselahs kindred more times than not... Garous (and other Fera) and the Technocracy, PROBABLY would clash more times and with more strenght than any others, even more than Union x Traditions and Garou x Pentex (both because they would hate each other, and because of kindred manipulation, who would hate both too). All that fighting would also probably bring Traditions+Seelie close to Garou+Dreamspeakers, if not as allies, but at least as non rival neutrals (no amount of mistrust is enough to keep factions as eternal enemies with a common enemy. Even the URSS allied with USA and UK against the nazi onslsught; to say that those relations wouldn't be formed between the denizens of WoD and that they would all behave and remain each one on their square is utterly nonsense)<br /> <br /> Not to mention that BSD, Baali and Malfean Nefandi would all be one big happy psychotic family","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T02:47:32-08:00","id":1056554,"title":"","content":"Family A sits down to meals, looks out the window and sees the back of a red house with no windows.<br /> <br /> Family B leaves for work and school every day and sees the front of a blue house with giant picture windows.<br /> <br /> This is the same house. Are they going to describe it the same way?<br /> <br /> Introducing 'consensus' into other games is like introducing 'generation' or 'spirit rank' to mages. Beyond possible minor impact on the gauntlet, what is there to introduce?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:52:46-08:00","id":1056786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056554#post1056554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Family A sits down to meals, looks out the window and sees the back of a red house with no windows.<br /> <br /> Family B leaves for work and school every day and sees the front of a blue house with giant picture windows.<br /> <br /> This is the same house. Are they going to describe it the same way?<br /> <br /> Introducing 'consensus' into other games is like introducing 'generation' or 'spirit rank' to mages. Beyond possible minor impact on the gauntlet, what is there to introduce?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf lore is... Just another Paradigm, one of many.<br /> <br /> PAM! You just killed WtA","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:53:43-08:00","id":1056787,"title":"","content":"Gaia is true.<br /> <br /> BANG! YOU killed Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T14:16:35-08:00","id":1056797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056495#post1056495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The consensus will definitely not work for Werewolf. Exactly why has been repeated many, many times. The moment you introduce consensus and subjective reality, W:tA leaves the building.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're definitely a Werewolf purist, so we won't agree on that, but I still don't think so. You just don't go with the &quot;consensus is everything&quot; model (that's why I stated they become incompatibel when taking to the extreme). What in Mage's cosmology excludes Gaia or the triat?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T14:46:58-08:00","id":1056805,"title":"","content":"Nothing. In fact, most of the factions in Mage align well with the Triat (Union = Weaver, Marauders = Wyld, and Nephandi = Wyrm). The Traditions would be independent of the Triat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T15:00:26-08:00","id":1056810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056797#post1056797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're definitely a Werewolf purist</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm taking the position that Mage's attempt to &quot;unify&quot; everything is actually not common ground, but a very Mage-specific interpretation of cosmology, much as how Demon's &quot;layers of reality&quot; is not actually a magic bullet to solve disputes. It's just Demon's specific way of setting up the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , so we won't agree on that, but I still don't think so. You just don't go with the &quot;consensus is everything&quot; model (that's why I stated they become incompatibel when taking to the extreme). What in Mage's cosmology excludes Gaia or the triat? </div> </div> </div>Its core thesis is the antithesis of Werewolf's core thesis, so there's that to start off with on a very wrong foot. How much space do you think &quot;humans don't deserve to be on a pedestal&quot; can share with &quot;humans should be able to define reality&quot;? Mage, at some point, always comes back to the proposition that Gaia isn't quite so important; in Werewolf, this isn't going to fly at all, and attempts to &quot;reconcile&quot; are going to be left hanging in some awkward space around the vicinity of character disempowerment and focus creep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T15:21:47-08:00","id":1056815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056810#post1056810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I'm taking the position that Mage's attempt to &quot;unify&quot; everything is actually not common ground, but a very Mage-specific interpretation of cosmology, much as how Demon's &quot;layers of reality&quot; is not actually a magic bullet to solve disputes. It's just Demon's specific way of setting up the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as the opposite of a Werewolf purist, I'm with this guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T15:41:25-08:00","id":1056822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056810#post1056810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its core thesis is the antithesis of Werewolf's core thesis, so there's that to start off with on a very wrong foot. How much space do you think &quot;humans don't deserve to be on a pedestal&quot; can share with &quot;humans should be able to define reality&quot;? Mage, at some point, always comes back to the proposition that Gaia isn't quite so important; in Werewolf, this isn't going to fly at all, and attempts to &quot;reconcile&quot; are going to be left hanging in some awkward space around the vicinity of character disempowerment and focus creep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although, that's not incompatibility in my eyes. Werewolves have a distinct view on things because of their connection to Gaia and the spirit world and mages are humans, so they tend to be human-centric but nothing says to me that the two could not exist in the same world. It's more of a difference between cultures and religions, IMO. <br /> <br /> That humans could alter reality (although not entirely defining it) doesn't equal with &quot;Gaia isn't important&quot;. Some mages might think so, others the opposite, still others just don't care.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T15:59:52-08:00","id":1056825,"title":"","content":"While the position of Mages may not necessarily disagree with the centrality of Gaia and the Trait, the Union (and many Craft and Traditions) cannot be correct of the WtA Lore is correct. Of course, they do not have to be correct for their True Magick to work or for Reality to function, and it really has no impact at all on cWoD if WtA Lore is correct and Mage Lore is incorrect.<br /> <br /> In fact, the mystical Traditions disagree with the idea of the centrality of the Consensus, which is they work best with other splats. The mystical Traditions (including the Order of Hermes) can easily accept and incorporate Gaia and the Triat into their cosmologies. That is because the mystical Traditions largely focus on understanding Reality as it is according to their Tradition before they use True Magic to change reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:26:38-08:00","id":1056837,"title":"","content":"Wow. I go to grade some papers, and this thread explodes.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056522#post1056522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is really simplistic, but more importantly, it's an incredibly tedious topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but I want to focus on this for a moment<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056356#post1056356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to beginning characters from the classic five gamelines, there is a pecking order. Ajaba, Bastet, Garou, Gurahl, Mokole, Nagah, and Rokea are the most powerful beginning characters. Ananasi, Corax, Kindred, Kitsune, KJ, Nuwushi, and Ratkin are the next most powerful beginning characters. Changelings and Mages are the second least powerful beginning characters. <b>Wraiths are the least powerful beginning characters.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>(emphasis mine) because WHAT THE FUCK? What fucking metric and rubric is this based on? But besides that, 1) white-room-power-level-ranking-tiers are bullshit, because there is no &quot;objectively best,&quot; and 2)Usury is a thing, right? Like, Monitors and their Arcanos are still around, yeah? Because Usury <i>will <b>absolutely</b></i> wreck the shit out of the above listed - because Usury lets a Wraith steal literal <i>Health Levels</i>, <u>and</u> gnosis/vitae/quintessence/glamour/whatever-the-fuck (at Storyteller discretion and a +3 difficulty).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:50:33-08:00","id":1056849,"title":"","content":"You have to 'physically' touch someone to use Usury (Wraith, p. 170), so you are probably going to have the crap kicked out of you by whatever you are attacking. Wraiths require extreme effort to effect the physical world, which why they are the least powerful beginning character. By contrast, a beginning Kindred can enslave a Wraith and a beginning Mage eat a Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:16:42-08:00","id":1056870,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> According to page 160 of <i>Wraith 2e</i>, Usury can be used in conjunction with Puppetry, so...<br /> <br /> Puppetry 1 and Usury X - the Wraith is now <i>literally inside the person</i> and siphoning health and magic juice. Usury can also be used during Embody, Inhabit, or Phamtasm. And <i>Buried Secrets</i> claims Puppetry and Usury both can be used on supernatural creatures - with no added difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:39:31-08:00","id":1056878,"title":"","content":"And my Kindred can still enslave them and my Mage can still eat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:39:39-08:00","id":1056879,"title":"","content":"Are we seriously trying to white room balance every splat in the game simultaneously? That may be the most White Wolf thing that has ever happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:50:52-08:00","id":1056887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056879#post1056879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we seriously trying to white room balance every splat in the game simultaneously? That may be the most White Wolf thing that has ever happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? Absurd - kind of like how I tried to demonstrate a starting Wraith that could eat people from the inside-out, supernaturals included, to prove that power-rankings are bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:10:24-08:00","id":1056902,"title":"","content":"Usury <i>is</i> pretty tight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:46:13-08:00","id":1056924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056786#post1056786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf lore is... Just another Paradigm, one of many.<br /> <br /> PAM! You just killed WtA</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056787#post1056787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia is true.<br /> <br /> BANG! YOU killed Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://pbs.twimg.com/media/CRrop6cWIAA3nzF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://pbs.twimg.com/media/CRrop6cWIAA3nzF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://pbs.twimg.com/media/CRrop6cWIAA3nzF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://pbs.twimg.com/media/CRrop6cWIAA3nzF.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Only if 'you', as a player or ST, take an in character perspective of the game lines and try to ham fist it onto everyone else at the table.<br /> <br /> Redneck Trees were made for those players.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056810#post1056810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its core thesis is the antithesis of Werewolf's core thesis, so there's that to start off with on a very wrong foot. How much space do you think &quot;humans don't deserve to be on a pedestal&quot; can share with &quot;humans should be able to define reality&quot;? Mage, at some point, always comes back to the proposition that Gaia isn't quite so important; in Werewolf, this isn't going to fly at all, and attempts to &quot;reconcile&quot; are going to be left hanging in some awkward space around the vicinity of character disempowerment and focus creep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that humans are VERY important in Werewolf. Maybe they <i>shouldn't</i> be. But the changing breeds have known they are, or at least would be (perhaps, in a self fullfilling prophecy), since the Impergium. And I'm pretty sure that even the least 'earthy' magical stylist (short of Infernalist) would say that the Earth dying would be a very bad thing for everyone, even if they never talked to a spirit or grew a tree.<br /> <br /> Every game line puts it's main protagonist at the center of the Universe.* Most characters believe the line and go with it. When playing a crossover, it is up to us, as players, to turn that drama into a compelling story with friends rather than letting it devolve into bickering as to which<b> fictional characters</b> are <u>right</u> about the <b>made up universe</b>,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *That used to be a real human belief amongst most people. In some parts of the world, <i>it still is</i>. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g84g2KJcUV0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g84g2KJcUV0</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T19:06:18-08:00","id":1056932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056810#post1056810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I'm taking the position that Mage's attempt to &amp;quot;unify&amp;quot; everything is actually not common ground, but a very Mage-specific interpretation of cosmology, much as how Demon's &amp;quot;layers of reality&amp;quot; is not actually a magic bullet to solve disputes. It's just Demon's specific way of setting up the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056810#post1056810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its core thesis is the antithesis of Werewolf's core thesis, so there's that to start off with on a very wrong foot. How much space do you think &quot;humans don't deserve to be on a pedestal&quot; can share with &quot;humans should be able to define reality&quot;. Mage, at some point, always comes back to the proposition that Gaia isn't quite so important; in Werewolf, this isn't going to fly at all, and attempts to &amp;quot;reconcile&amp;quot; are going to be left hanging in some awkward space around the vicinity of character disempowerment and focus creep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, its like I said, you can either have Gaia or Consensus, but NOT both.<br /> <br /> Maybe, the closest thing we could do to mend those two (the two troublemakers of WoD, Werewolf and Mage), perhaps its the discussion on &quot;Reality Principles&quot; we had on the Mage forum, because it does say that Consensus can only be achieved by the totality of beings on the Tellurian, meaning that some gazillions of spirits are far more relevant than some few billions of humans, reality is subjective but no one could tell, because it is higly kept by inercia (some trillions of gravity spirits will prevent any attempt of humans trying to subvert it), and Gaia has a major relevance (as does the Triat), after all Gaia (and its trillions upon trillions upon trillions) of spirits is responsible for its &quot;Gaian Consensus&quot; just like the Wyrm is responsible for the &quot;Entropic Consensus&quot; and so. Its a subjective reality that, as Aya said, becomes &quot;mere academic curiosity&quot;. And, no &quot; humans are special&quot;. Just &quot;humans are adaptable&quot;, meaning: you COULD convince trillions of gravity spirits to reverse gravity (change their &quot;consensual notion&quot; of it). However, spirits are too deep in their core concepts, they cant change easily. Humans, however, are NOT so defined, they can be molded. So, an anger spirit will always be anger. An anger human can find inner peace. Despite that, humans AREN'T the force that keep the balance in the world. Spirits are. And... They still can change things. A sweetly beautiful Paradox. How's that for ya?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T19:28:14-08:00","id":1056937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056825#post1056825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the position of Mages may not necessarily disagree with the centrality of Gaia and the Trait, the Union (and many Craft and Traditions) cannot be correct of the WtA Lore is correct. Of course, they do not have to be correct for their True Magick to work or for Reality to function, and it really has no impact at all on cWoD if WtA Lore is correct and Mage Lore is incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as it has absolutely ZERO impact for WoD if WtA lore is incorrect. Stop thinking your favorite splat is the best thing in the world since soap because its NOT true, no matter how much you like (just like I dont think that Mage should be the supremme game of WoD. So please, stop it right there)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056825#post1056825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, the mystical Traditions disagree with the idea of the centrality of the Consensus, which is they work best with other splats. The mystical Traditions (including the Order of Hermes) can easily accept and incorporate Gaia and the Triat into their cosmologies. That is because the mystical Traditions largely focus on understanding Reality as it is according to their Tradition before they use True Magic to change reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, where da hell do you get that shit? The Traditions understand the Consensus just as fine as the Technocracy, THAT'S THE WHOLE FUCKING POINT OF THE ASCENSION WAR!!!<br /> <br /> Besides, lets see a few of those Traditions that &quot;incorporates Gaia&quot;:<br /> <br /> Hermetics - all humans have the divine spark.<br /> Chorus - we were made by the one (Gaia is just another false icon)<br /> VA - What Gaia?<br /> Eutanathoi - Its all the wheel.<br /> Extatics - Its all an ilusion. Including your primitive godess<br /> Sons of Ether - Gaia? Do you the mother of the olympians of the greek myth?<br /> Dreamspeakers - spirits are everything. You say Gaia is their boss? Well, I dont know about that, but we must restore balance<br /> Verbena - the Goddess have many faces and many names. It isnt however, a jorney for the Goddess outside, but rather, a jorney towards your inner Goddess.<br /> <br /> Please dude, WtA lore is the lore of Werewolf. Period. Stop dealing with it as if all other splats should embrace it.<br /> <br /> I just remembered: remember that one time that YOU basically told me to shut up, because, since it was a discussion about Werewolf, WtA lore were supremme and I didn't had the right to talk about it? Yeah... Because I remember that quite well.<br /> <br /> So, since you're talking about MageMage lore, Now its time to repay in kind Aya (as I knew this time would come, inevitable)... Do NOT, I repeat, do NOT talk about Mage lore. When playing MAGE, you just takes Consensus as it is AND TRASH GAIA OR THE TRIAT. PERIOD.<br /> <br /> (Next time dont be so authoritarian when someone questions something about werewolf and you won't have to deal with this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T19:40:16-08:00","id":1056944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056924#post1056924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://pbs.twimg.com/media/CRrop6cWIAA3nzF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://pbs.twimg.com/media/CRrop6cWIAA3nzF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://pbs.twimg.com/media/CRrop6cWIAA3nzF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://pbs.twimg.com/media/CRrop6cWIAA3nzF.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Only if 'you', as a player or ST, take an in character perspective of the game lines and try to ham fist it onto everyone else at the table.<br /> <br /> Redneck Trees were made for those players.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except that humans are VERY important in Werewolf. Maybe they <i>shouldn't</i> be. But the changing breeds have known they are, or at least would be (perhaps, in a self fullfilling prophecy), since the Impergium. And I'm pretty sure that even the least 'earthy' magical stylist (short of Infernalist) would say that the Earth dying would be a very bad thing for everyone, even if they never talked to a spirit or grew a tree.<br /> <br /> Every game line puts it's main protagonist at the center of the Universe.* Most characters believe the line and go with it. When playing a crossover, it is up to us, as players, to turn that drama into a compelling story with friends rather than letting it devolve into bickering as to which<b> fictional characters</b> are <u>right</u> about the <b>made up universe</b>,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *That used to be a real human belief amongst most people. In some parts of the world, <i>it still is</i>. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g84g2KJcUV0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g84g2KJcUV0</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Its NOT about Byzantine theological discussions between splats. Its about - is technology just some weird collective belief, or is it something of the Weaver? Because THAT has an absolutely impact in the game (werolves can use cellphones just fine in Amazonia, technocrats cant). <br /> <br /> And, once again, the Technocracy is either mighty or isn't nothing. And Mage without them is just that crap Awakening. So, it doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T19:43:54-08:00","id":1056946,"title":"","content":"Those differences have profound impacts on game play that goes way beyond personal beliefs of the chars. So, no, its not just because the Garou will many kill the MAGE because he is a zealoty fanatical that things that Mages are disrupters of Gaia, but because there are many changes in the scenario that totally disfugures both games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T19:45:16-08:00","id":1056947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056924#post1056924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except that humans are VERY important in Werewolf. Maybe they <i>shouldn't</i> be. But the changing breeds have known they are, or at least would be (perhaps, in a self fullfilling prophecy), since the Impergium. And I'm pretty sure that even the least 'earthy' magical stylist (short of Infernalist) would say that the Earth dying would be a very bad thing for everyone, even if they never talked to a spirit or grew a tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a matter of impact, but of thematic allocation. In Werewolf, humanity is very clearly in the wrong as a whole, and they shouldn't be expanding beyond modest bounds and necessitating that the Ratkin take drastic action. Mage never really questions humanity's right to alter of the world around it, just whether or not you can get people to believe in it, and would be aghast to have Ratkin take just about any action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T23:53:25-08:00","id":1057006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050909-many-wods-vs-single-wod?p=1056937#post1056937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, since you're talking about MageMage lore, Now its time to repay in kind Aya (as I knew this time would come, inevitable)... Do NOT, I repeat, do NOT talk about Mage lore. When playing MAGE, you just takes Consensus as it is AND TRASH GAIA OR THE TRIAT. PERIOD.<br /> <br /> (Next time dont be so authoritarian when someone questions something about werewolf and you won't have to deal with this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No one is going to have to deal with this. You have repeatedly demonstrated you are not a good fit for this forum community so your posting privileges are being permanently suspended.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T10:26:36-08:00","id":1057145,"title":"","content":"Just to say it: The &quot;Consensus it's Everything&quot; it's not an extremist posture to portray the setting. The &quot;Consensus it's Everything&quot; it's the first thing you read when you open a Mage Basic. It's the core of it's cosmology.<br /> And this isn't about what mages believe, many mages believe otherwise (like, all young technocrats that wrongly believe that their science it's not the magick of the traditions but something demonstrable, while their Masters know better), but the game strongly implies that All of Reality get's defined by entities with Avatar (aka. Humans)<br /> <br /> While you can take some paragraphs of lore here and there to justify a not-so Dynamic Reality that's still &quot;mage friendly&quot;, practically everything in Mage, even Mythic Threads and Foundations gets explained with the suggestion that even these things are product of the Consensus (the universal subconscious, things that are so ingrained that nobody questions, etc.)<br /> <br /> To say that you MUST depart from the idea that &quot;Reality it's Consensual&quot; to ST a Good Crossover game it's proff enough of how damaging crossover it's to the games involved. Namely, in the One WoD one of the core premises of a game it's objectively false, it's use in game gets discouraged (unless it's just a wrong IOC oppinion, and not something that will literally enter in game sooner or latter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T12:23:09-08:00","id":1057181,"title":"","content":"A key difference to realize why it's hard to equal-lore crossover Mage (And Mage specifically) with other gamelines, is that the Mage gameline inverts the usual WoD in-character/out-of-character lore formula.<br /> Here's a simplified example:<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampire:<br /> &quot;<i>European vampires *believe* that vampirism is God's punishment on Caine. They *believe* that they are descendants from him, and some treat it as a sin to escape, others embrace it. Nordic vikings *believe* they are descendants from a warrior blessed by Odin. An African bloodline *believes* that they got created from love between one of theirs and a witch.<br /> What's true? Who knows, maybe they are all wrong. Up to the ST. It might be an endgame thing the characters discover.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Mage:<br /> &quot;<i>What your characters believe? Come up with something fitting to your style. Have fun. Here are a lot of examples to help you though.<br /> Here are the hard facts though: Reality gets shaped by humanity's belief, and all that awakened Mages do is pure willworking, no matter what they *think* they are doing.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Notice the reversal?<br /> In a game like Vampire, the game goes out of its way to create a rich in-game lore for a small set of beliefs that most characters stick to, while keeping the actual truth ultimately up for grabs.<br /> In Mage, the beliefs of the characters are up to the player to come up with and get creative at, they can be all over the place from the mundane to the absolutely freaky and outworldly without any established limits. But the game establishes the basic out-of-character facts of the world that the characters might not even ever accept to believe in.<br /> <br /> In both games, doing a crossover won't change anything in-game from the character's point of view at all. That's not the issue.<br /> They will still have their same opinions, belief systems and experiences. Same old, same old. However, while Vampire never establishes out-of-character Truth with a capital T (Aside of some of the endgame Gehenna book scenarios I guess) and thus does not really suffer OOCly from equal-lore crossovers, putting another game's lore on par with that of the Mage game in a crossover changes hard, out-of-character core concepts of the mage gameline's world.<br /> <br /> That's the big difficulty, and why so many Mage players react poorly to the idea of single-WoD crossovers. Hope that helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-02-2017, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T09:21:15-08:00","id":1057623,"title":"","content":"Still, Gehenna scenarios exist. I may want to use the Antediluvians as narrative tools to end the world, thus I want that to be a potential outcome.<br /> <br /> It's important to keep these things open. If in the One Wod it's *stated* that there's much more powerful beings than the Antes, that can and will impede the end of the world as we know it, then that narrative tool it's lost. Or at least it's not present, I mean, I know that I can do whatever I want with the lore, but the lore it's there to give you options. I didn't invented the Gehena concept, it was presented to me. And I think it was cool.<br /> If the rumors about 5th edition are true, then Gehena seems to have had a smaller impact in vampire society than the Anarch Revolt. I don't know you people, but that wasn't what I bought when Vampire sold me the Gehena.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, the Consensus it's important to Mage. Not as a belief held by the characters, but as a posibility, a basis to build the setting.<br /> It's part of Mage spirit, and while I mantain that there is both OOC and IOC Mage lore that points to the idea that maybe not all of Reality it's Consensual, I also think that the concept, as a core and loved concept of Mage, shouldn't be left aside to create One WoD (or, at least, shouldn't be treated as a minor sacrifice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-03-2017, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T23:25:33-08:00","id":1057950,"title":"","content":"Mage is my favorite gameline, but I will definitely admit that Mages are the <i>worst</i> in crossovers to other gamelines. Sorcerers fit in the other games much better. Also I think Sorcerers as they are written are terrible in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T07:20:45-08:00","id":1058032,"title":"","content":"Sorcerers are definitely good in a number of games as medium-level allies/enemies. Infernal Sorcerers are good as high-level allies/enemies. Just because a woman sacrifices a man every Beltane to Ishtar and turns him into spicy sausage for her snacks for the rest of the year does not mean that you cannot work with her (especially if she is sacrificing and eating only child molesters, rapists, and slavers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}